t["npc:gornek"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="6,204,22.613.0,28.513.0,14.190.0,24.155.0,34.221.0,34.207.0",["h"]="5221a5",["n"]="Gornek",["s"]="Gornek. Gornek es un capataz orco apostado en el Valle de los Retos, en Durotar. Actúa como el principal punto de recepción para los nuevos reclutas orcos y trols Lanza Negra que se disponen a demostrar su valía ante la nueva Horda. Apostado justo en el corazón del Valle de los Retos, Gornek representa la prueba inicial de disciplina para los aspirantes a guerreros, exploradores y lanzadores de conjuros de la Horda. Por orden del Jefe de Guerra Thrall, cada joven y recién llegado debe ganarse su lugar mediante el tesón y la perseverancia, y no por derecho de cuna. Gornek evalúa a quienes entran en el valle leyendo sus órdenes de presentación y dirigiéndolos a los instructores del recinto. Ya lleve el iniciado un garabato cifrado, un Glyphic Parchment o una Tablilla sencilla, es Gornek quien recibe sus credenciales y los encamina en su dura senda de supervivencia.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["race:Orc"]="For young orcs, reporting to Gornek is the very first step toward shedding childhood and earning an honorable place in Durotar.",["race:Troll"]="As allies sheltered by Thrall, Darkspear trolls present their credentials to Gornek to prove they stand as capable equals alongside their orc brothers."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Gornek is an orc greeter and taskmaster in the Valley of Trials. He oversees new recruits of the Horde, reading their induction documents and guiding them to their respective class trainers.",["al"]={"gornek","who is this orc","who is gornek"},["q"]="Who is Gornek?"},{["a"]="He stands near the center of the Valley of Trials in southwestern Durotar, just outside the Den where young orcs and Darkspear trolls begin their journeys.",["al"]={"gornek location","where is gornek","gornek map"},["q"]="Where can I find Gornek?"},{["a"]="New arrivals carry training scrolls and tablets designating their chosen discipline. Gornek evaluates these letters of introduction, confirms their eligibility, and sends them to the appropriate mentors within the valley.",["al"]={"why visit gornek","parchment quest","tablet quest"},["q"]="Why do new recruits report to him?"},{["a"]="He acts as an entry coordinator for Thrall's New Horde. His duty is to ensure no recruit enters the broader lands of Durotar without first learning the basic tenets of honor, survival, and martial readiness.",["al"]={"gornek horde role","what does gornek do"},["q"]="What is his role in the New Horde?"}},["kw"]={"den","durotar","gornek","parchment","the new horde","valley of trials"},["n"]="Gornek",["s"]="Gornek is an orc overseer stationed in the Valley of Trials in Durotar. He serves as the primary point of intake for fresh orc and Darkspear troll recruits preparing to prove their worth to the New Horde.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Standing directly at the heart of the Valley of Trials, Gornek represents the initial test of discipline for aspiring Horde warriors, scouts, and spellcasters. Under Warchief Thrall's order, every youth and newcomer must earn their place through grit and perseverance rather than entitlement. Gornek assesses those stepping into the valley, reading their introductory orders and directing them to trainers throughout the compound. Whether an initiate carries an encrypted scrawl, a glyphic parchment, or a simple tablet, it is Gornek who receives their credentials and sets them upon their harsh path of survival.",["t"]="Welcoming the Unproven"},{["b"]="The arid canyons of the valley test more than battle prowess; they instill the communal ethos of the New Horde. Gornek ensures that novices do not linger aimlessly, pointing them toward the trials of the nearby scorpid burrows, the dens of feral boars, and the watchful eyes of veteran instructors. For those who survive the training grounds and slay the threats lurking in the red rock gullies, Gornek offers the final acknowledgment before dispatching them outward into the wider, perilous landscape of Durotar.",["t"]="A Life in Service to Durotar"}}}}}
t["npc:grelin-whitebeard"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,309,15.563.0,20.567.0,46.284.0,27.207.0,24.228.0,31.146.0,56.221.0,46.184.0",["h"]="5a4b46",["n"]="Grelin Barbablanca",["s"]="Grelin Barbablanca. Grelin Barbablanca es un explorador enano apostado en el Valle de Crestanevada por decreto real para evaluar la amenaza de los troles Melenafreche. Desde un campamento aislado y junto a un aprendiz torpe, depende de los nuevos aventureros para mantener a raya a los troles mientras la atención de Forjaz sigue consumida por la crisis de los troggs. Grelin Barbablanca y su hermano Senir fueron enviados al Valle de Crestanevada bajo órdenes directas del Senado de Forjaz y del mismísimo Rey Magni Barbabronce. Su misión era clara: evaluar y neutralizar la amenaza que suponían los troles Melenafreche autóctonos. Con el ejército oficial de Forjaz totalmente empantanado combatiendo los brotes de troggs por todo Dun Morogh, los hermanos recibieron muy pocos recursos para cumplir su cometido. Grelin tuvo que establecer un puesto en las colinas nevadas y recurrir a reclutas locales y a los iniciados que pasaban por allí para llevar a cabo el trabajo necesario.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Grelin's plight reveals just how thin the Alliance and Ironforge armies are stretched in Dun Morogh, forcing solitary scouts to wage quiet wars against troll enclaves.",["race:Dwarf"]="Serving King Magni directly, Grelin represents the quiet, stubborn perseverance of Ironforge scouts holding Dun Morogh's borders together against mounting internal threats.",["race:Gnome"]="Fresh out of Gnomeregan's tragedy, gnome refugees passing through Coldridge Valley find Grelin working alongside a wandering gnome at his remote camp."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Grelin was officially commissioned by the Senate of Ironforge and King Magni Bronzebeard to investigate and quell the Frostmane troll threat in Coldridge Valley. Because the dwarven military is tied down fighting the trogg menace elsewhere, Grelin must rely on independent volunteers.",["al"]={"why is grelin here","grelin whitebeard purpose","who is grelin whitebeard"},["q"]="Why is Grelin Whitebeard out here in the snow?"},{["a"]="A Frostmane troll named Grik'nir the Cold raided Grelin's camp while it was left unattended. Grelin only caught a glimpse of a heavily marked brute fleeing into the southern troll caves with his field notes.",["al"]={"who stole the journal","stolen journal thief","grelin journal"},["q"]="Who stole Grelin's journal?"},{["a"]="His brother is Senir Whitebeard, an operative stationed further down the mountain in the town of Kharanos. Grelin compiles his findings on troll movements into reports and sends trusted runners to deliver them directly to Senir.",["al"]={"grelin brother","senir whitebeard","who is senir"},["q"]="Who is Grelin's brother?"},{["a"]="Grelin shares his small encampment with an absent-minded dwarven apprentice, leaving him with little competent help until capable recruits arrive.",["al"]={"whitebeard camp npcs","who is with grelin","grelin companions"},["q"]="Who is with Grelin at his camp?"},{["a"]="Ironforge's defenders and Senate forces are almost entirely consumed by the widespread trogg infestations that have erupted across Dun Morogh. This leaves scouts like Grelin to solve regional threats using local recruits.",["al"]={"why no dwarven army","where is the ironforge guard","why no soldiers"},["q"]="Why doesn't Ironforge send regular soldiers to help him?"},{["a"]="Jona Ironstock is an old and trusted friend of Grelin. Stationed near the starting grounds of Coldridge Valley, Jona helps direct new dwarven and gnomish recruits toward Grelin's camp.",["al"]={"grelin and jona","jona ironstock"},["q"]="What is Grelin's connection to Jona Ironstock?"}},["kw"]={"coldridge valley","dun morogh","frostmane","grelin whitebeard","grik'nir","ironforge senate","senir whitebeard","the stolen journal"},["n"]="Grelin Whitebeard",["s"]="Grelin Whitebeard is a dwarven scout stationed in Coldridge Valley by royal decree to assess the Frostmane troll threat. Operating out of an isolated camp with a bumbling apprentice, he relies on rising adventurers to keep the trolls contained while Ironforge's attention remains consumed by the trogg crisis.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Grelin Whitebeard and his brother Senir were dispatched to Coldridge Valley under direct orders from the Senate of Ironforge and King Magni Bronzebeard himself. Their mission was clear: assess and neutralize the threat posed by the native Frostmane trolls. With Ironforge's official military fully bogged down combating trogg outbreaks across Dun Morogh, the brothers were given very few resources to accomplish their task. Grelin had to establish an outpost in the snowy hills and look toward local recruits and passing initiates to carry out the necessary work.",["t"]="A Royal Mandate"},{["b"]="From his camp, Grelin monitors the encroaching Frostmane tribe south of Coldridge Valley. The trolls have grown increasingly aggressive, staging bolder incursions outside their mountain caverns. During one such raid, a heavily painted brute named Grik'nir the Cold slipped into the unattended camp and made off with Grelin's field journal, containing his critical observations. Unwilling to fail the King, Grelin uses intrepid travelers to strike deep into the Frostmane caves, recover his stolen writings, and ensure his final intelligence reaches Senir in Kharanos.",["t"]="Trouble in the South"}}}}}
t["npc:grif-wildheart"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,424,19.495.0,20.507.0,24.472.0,22.187.0,32.138.0,36.200.0,43.152.0,66.188.0,49.198.0",["h"]="25a82b",["n"]="Grif Corazón Salvaje",["s"]="Grif Corazón Salvaje. Grif Corazón Salvaje es un experimentado instructor de cazadores enano apostado en el exterior de la Destilería Cebatruenos en Kharanos. Célebre entre los montañeros locales por su profunda afinidad con la fauna, instruye a los tiradores noveles en rastreo, puntería y los ritos de doma de bestias. Para los jóvenes cazadores que emergen del Valle de Crestanevada, Grif ofrece el puente vital entre disparar un rifle y caminar junto a un leal compañero animal. Mientras muchos enanos de Forjaz prefieren el calor ardiente de una forja o el repiqueteo constante de los picos, Grif Corazón Salvaje ha dedicado su vida por entero a la gélida naturaleza de Dun Morogh. Los montañeros locales bromean diciendo que pasa demasiado tiempo con bestias de cuatro patas, pero nadie discute su dominio de lo salvaje. Tras pasar años rastreando a lo largo de crestas nevadas junto a veteranos compañeros de caza, Grif posee un conocimiento íntimo de los depredadores naturales que merodean por los riscos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Hunter"]="Grif is the essential mentor who initiates Alliance hunters into beast taming, offering the vital quests that allow you to bond with wild predators across Dun Morogh.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stationed in Kharanos, Grif prepares Alliance scouts and sharpshooters to survive the harsh wilderness surrounding the mountain kingdom of Ironforge.",["race:Dwarf"]="Embodying the dwarven mountaineer tradition, Grif shows how a dwarf's rugged resilience makes them exceptionally suited for living side-by-side with wild mountain beasts."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Grif Wildheart is a dwarven hunter trainer located in Kharanos in Dun Morogh. He serves as the primary mentor for novice Alliance hunters learning their trade outside of Coldridge Valley.",["al"]={"who is grif","grif wildheart identity","about grif"},["q"]="Who is Grif Wildheart?"},{["a"]="He stands outside near the Thunderbrew Distillery in the village of Kharanos, along the snowy road connecting Coldridge Pass to Ironforge.",["al"]={"grif wildheart location","where is grif","grif in kharanos"},["q"]="Where can I find Grif Wildheart?"},{["a"]="Beyond offering general hunter abilities and ranged combat techniques, Grif guides young hunters through the trials of beast taming, teaching them to soothe and master wild boars, leopards, and bears.",["al"]={"what does grif teach","grif hunter training","grif skills"},["q"]="What does Grif teach novice hunters?"},{["a"]="Grif charges his students with tracking down and taming three specific creatures of Dun Morogh: a Large Crag Boar, a Snow Leopard, and an Ice Claw Bear.",["al"]={"grif taming quests","which animals to tame dun morogh","taming the beast targets"},["q"]="What beasts does Grif send hunters to tame?"},{["a"]="After proving their ability to tame wild animals, Grif directs hunters to travel into the city of Ironforge to consult with advanced beast trainers about feeding and commanding their pets.",["al"]={"where after grif","training the beast next step","grif follow up quest"},["q"]="Where does Grif send hunters after completing their taming trials?"},{["a"]="The local Ironforge Mountaineers note that Grif spends a bit too much time in the company of animals rather than people, but they readily admit he knows the hunter's craft better than almost anyone.",["al"]={"mountaineer opinion of grif","is grif respected","grif reputation"},["q"]="What do the Ironforge mountaineers think of Grif?"}},["kw"]={"beast taming","dun morogh","grif wildheart","hunter trainer","kharanos","mountaineer","taming the beast","thunderbrew distillery"},["n"]="Grif Wildheart",["s"]="Grif Wildheart is a seasoned dwarven hunter trainer stationed outside the Thunderbrew Distillery in Kharanos. Renowned among the local mountaineers for his deep affinity with wildlife, he instructs budding marksmen in tracking, marksmanship, and the rites of beast taming. For young hunters emerging from Coldridge Valley, Grif provides the vital bridge between firing a rifle and walking alongside a loyal animal companion.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While many Ironforge dwarves prefer the fiery warmth of a forge or the steady clink of pickaxes, Grif Wildheart has dedicated his life entirely to the frozen wilderness of Dun Morogh. Local mountaineers half-jokingly say he spends a bit too much time with four-legged beasts, but none dispute his mastery of the wild. Having spent years tracking across snowbound ridges alongside seasoned hunting companions, Grif possesses an intimate understanding of the natural predators that roam the crags.",["t"]="A Life in the Wilds"},{["b"]="When young dwarf hunters finish their preliminary trials in Coldridge Valley, they are directed straight to Kharanos to seek Grif's guidance. While he sharpens their aim and teaches essential wilderness survival tricks, his true specialty lies in forging bonds between hunter and beast. Through a sequence of rigorous trials, Grif sends his pupils out into the freezing wastes with a taming rod to test their mettle against Dun Morogh's iconic predators: Large Crag Boars, Snow Leopards, and Ice Claw Bears.",["t"]="The Way of the Beast"},{["b"]="Once a hunter demonstrates the will and composure needed to calm three distinct wild beasts, Grif's tutelage in Kharanos reaches its conclusion. Recognizing that a hunter must also learn to feed, discipline, and train their new ally, he sends his graduates up the mountainside to Ironforge. There, under the great vaulted roofs of the dwarven capital, novice hunters report to master beast trainers to learn the deeper art of caring for their permanent lifelong companion.",["t"]="Journey to the High Seat"}}}}}
t["npc:gryan-stoutmantle"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,298,22.599.0,20.546.0,21.617.1,25.178.0,68.259.0,45.247.0,47.290.0,52.281.1,32.245.0",["h"]="94c7a1",["n"]="Gryan Mantorrecio",["s"]="Gryan Mantorrecio. Gryan Mantorrecio es un paladín de la Mano de Plata y el comandante de Las Milicias del Pueblo, que opera desde Colina del Centinela en Páramos de Poniente. Nacido en Páramos de Poniente, regresó del devastado reino norteño de Lordaeron para proteger su tierra natal después de que la corona de Ventormenta abandonara la región al bandidaje. Gryan Mantorrecio comenzó su servicio lejos de los tranquilos campos del sur de Azeroth. Viajando al norte hacia Lordaeron en su juventud, tomó los votos como Caballero de la Mano de Plata y soportó los horrores de la Tercera Guerra, presenciando incluso la trágica purga de Stratholme a manos del príncipe Arthas Menethil. Cuando le llegaron noticias de que su provincia natal de Páramos de Poniente se estaba hundiendo en la anarquía, asolada por bandidos organizados y abandonada por la corona, Gryan dejó atrás los frentes del norte. Cambió los campos de batalla imperiales por la defensa de campesinos honrados, jurando que su hogar no caería como lo había hecho el norte.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,1,0},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Paladin"]="Stoutmantle is a living example of Silver Hand duty: when the high councils of church and crown ignored the poor, he brought the Light's protection directly to the humble farmers who needed it most.",["faction:Alliance"]="Gryan's reliance on independent volunteers exposes the bitter cracks within the Alliance heartland, where political inaction in Stormwind forces loyal citizens to take up their own arms.",["race:Human"]="Born in Westfall, Gryan represents the resilience of Stormwind's rural folk, standing firm against both regional brigands and bureaucratic abandonment by the capital."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Gryan Stoutmantle is a paladin of the Silver Hand and the founder and commander of the People's Militia, the volunteer garrison headquartered at Sentinel Hill defending Westfall.",["al"]={"who is gryan","stoutmantle lore","leader of westfall"},["q"]="Who is Gryan Stoutmantle?"},{["a"]="Stormwind's House of Nobles refused to commit crown soldiers or treasury funds to protect the outlying province. Left to fend for themselves against marauders and gnolls, the local peasantry under Gryan's leadership formed their own independent defense force.",["al"]={"why militia","where is stormwind army","why did stormwind abandon westfall"},["q"]="Why is the People's Militia needed if Westfall belongs to Stormwind?"},{["a"]="Gryan traveled to Lordaeron in his youth to become a holy paladin of the Silver Hand. He served on northern battlefields during the Third War and was present during the culling of Stratholme before departing south to rescue his imperiled homeland.",["al"]={"is gryan a paladin","gryan silver hand","gryan in lordaeron"},["q"]="What is Gryan's history with the Silver Hand?"},{["a"]="When Magistrate Solomon of Lakeshire requested reinforcements against Redridge's gnolls and orcs, Gryan was forced to decline. The People's Militia is stretched to its absolute breaking point holding Sentinel Hill; sending even a small detachment would cause Westfall to fall to the Defias.",["al"]={"magistrate solomon request","help redridge","why no troops to lakeshire"},["q"]="Why does Gryan refuse to send aid to Lakeshire?"},{["a"]="With intelligence from Wiley the Black and SI:7 spymaster Mathias Shaw, Gryan unmasked Edwin VanCleef as the mastermind. The militia then captured a thief known as the Defias Traitor, who guided Alliance forces straight to the Brotherhood's base in the Deadmines beneath Moonbrook.",["al"]={"finding deadmines","who found vancleef","defias traitor story"},["q"]="How did Gryan discover where the Defias were hiding?"},{["a"]="Wiley the Black is a contact living at the inn in Lakeshire who owed his life to Gryan. Although Stoutmantle holds little affection for the rogue's unsavory nature, he leveraged that life debt to obtain crucial intelligence on Defias operations.",["al"]={"wiley and gryan","wiley the black debt"},["q"]="Who is Wiley the Black to Gryan?"}},["kw"]={"deadmines","gryan","people's militia","sentinel hill","silver hand","stoutmantle","vancleef","westfall","wiley"},["n"]="Gryan Stoutmantle",["s"]="Gryan Stoutmantle is a paladin of the Silver Hand and the commander of the People's Militia, operating out of Sentinel Hill in Westfall. Born in Westfall, he returned from the devastated northern kingdom of Lordaeron to protect his homeland after Stormwind's crown abandoned the region to banditry.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Gryan Stoutmantle began his service far from the quiet fields of southern Azeroth. Traveling north to Lordaeron as a young man, he took vows as a Knight of the Silver Hand and endured the horrors of the Third War, even witnessing the tragic purge of Stratholme by Prince Arthas Menethil. When news reached him that his native province of Westfall was collapsing into lawlessness, overrun by organized brigands and abandoned by the crown, Gryan left the northern fronts behind. He traded imperial battlefields for the defense of honest farmers, swearing that his home would not fall as the north had.",["t"]="A Knight Returned Home"},{["b"]="Upon his return, Gryan found Westfall virtually undefended. Due to royal neglect and political paralysis within the House of Nobles, Stormwind refused to dispatch garrison troops. In response, Stoutmantle established the People's Militia at Sentinel Hill, rallying local farmers, sentries, and traveling mercenaries into a volunteer defense corps. His forces hold a precarious line against the Defias Brotherhood, riverpaw gnolls, and hostile mechanoids, unable even to spare reinforcements when neighbor settlements like Lakeshire plead for aid.",["t"]="The People's Militia"},{["b"]="Refusing to fight blindly, Stoutmantle turned to an extensive intelligence network to uncover who was orchestrating Westfall's ruin. Calling in an old debt from the shady rogue Wiley the Black in Redridge and conferring with Mathias Shaw of SI:7, Gryan pierced the veil: the bandits were led by Edwin VanCleef, the slighted master architect of the Stonemasons' Guild. After the militia captured a bandit attempting to plunder a local wagon, Gryan used the traitor to pinpoint the Brotherhood's headquarters hidden beneath Moonbrook within the Deadmines, tasking veteran champions with striking down VanCleef directly.",["t"]="Unmasking the Kingpin"}}}}}
t["npc:guard-thomas"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="12,261,21.542.0,17.495.1,30.142.0,45.258.0,53.251.0,43.251.0,32.275.0,75.208.0",["h"]="38e89b",["n"]="Guardia Thomas",["s"]="Guardia Thomas. El Guardia Thomas es un devoto soldado del ejército de Ventormenta destinado en el puente al oeste del Aserradero de la Vega del Este. Aislado en la frontera oriental del Bosque de Elwynn, supervisa la defensa de los colonos locales frente a la fauna depredadora y a los múrlocs invasores. Mientras gran parte de la atención del reino se centra hacia el interior, hacia la capital, o hacia el oeste, hacia los Páramos de Poniente, el Guardia Thomas ocupa uno de los puestos más tranquilos pero a la vez más precarios del Bosque de Elwynn. Situado en el puente de piedra que cruza el río hacia el Aserradero de la Vega del Este, Thomas constituye una frágil línea de defensa entre los trabajadores forestales y las agresivas criaturas que merodean por los bosques. Con las fuerzas militares de Ventormenta al límite de su capacidad, guardias como Thomas deben depender enormemente de los aventureros que pasan por allí para mantener el orden y llevar mensajes al mando central.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warrior"]="For young warriors of the Alliance, Thomas represents frontline discipline and the unglamorous realities of regional border defense.",["faction:Alliance"]="Guard Thomas embodies the overstretched state of the Stormwind Army, holding a vital outpost on the frontier with minimal support from the crown."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Guard Thomas is posted on the stone bridge spanning the river just west of the Eastvale Logging Camp, along the eastern road in Elwynn Forest.",["al"]={"guard thomas location","where is thomas","guard thomas bridge"},["q"]="Where can I find Guard Thomas?"},{["a"]="He is an officer of the Stormwind Army assigned to protect the eastern frontier of Elwynn. His responsibilities include securing the trade bridge, defending nearby workers from wild predators, and monitoring hostile murloc encroachments along the riverbanks.",["al"]={"what does thomas do","guard thomas role","thomas eastvale"},["q"]="What is Guard Thomas's duty in Elwynn Forest?"},{["a"]="Routine patrols dispatched into the river basins have failed to report back. Without sufficient reinforcements to leave his post unmanned, Thomas enlists traveling adventurers to search the waterways and find out what happened to his missing comrades.",["al"]={"lost guards elwynn","guard thomas missing scouts","what happened to the guards"},["q"]="Why is Guard Thomas asking for help with lost guards?"},{["a"]="Murloc tribes have increasingly crept up the river systems of eastern Elwynn. Their growing presence threatens both local logging operations and overland supply routes, prompting Thomas to place open bounties on their fins to keep the waterways clear.",["al"]={"murlocs eastvale","why kill murlocs","guard thomas murloc bounty"},["q"]="Why are murlocs a problem for Guard Thomas?"},{["a"]="Thomas serves within the Stormwind Army, reporting through the military hierarchy back to regional command in Goldshire and the capital. As matters deteriorate across the borders, his dispatches also coordinate with frontier leadership like Gryan Stoutmantle out in Westfall.",["al"]={"thomas superior","stormwind army chain of command","who does thomas work for"},["q"]="Who does Guard Thomas report to?"},{["a"]="Once the immediate threats around Eastvale and the eastern river are handled, Thomas provides reports directing seasoned travelers toward Westfall to aid Gryan Stoutmantle and the struggling People's Militia.",["al"]={"after guard thomas","where to go after eastvale","westfall report"},["q"]="Where does Guard Thomas send adventurers once their work in Elwynn is done?"}},["kw"]={"eastvale","eastvale logging camp","elwynn forest","guard thomas","lost guards","murloc","stormwind army","thomas"},["n"]="Guard Thomas",["s"]="Guard Thomas is a dedicated soldier of the Stormwind Army stationed at the bridge west of the Eastvale Logging Camp. Isolated on the eastern frontier of Elwynn Forest, he oversees the defense of local settlers against predatory wildlife and encroaching murlocs.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While much of the realm's attention is focused inward toward the capital or west toward Westfall, Guard Thomas holds one of the quietest yet most precarious posts in Elwynn Forest. Positioned at the stone bridge crossing the river toward Eastvale Logging Camp, Thomas acts as the thin blue line between everyday forestry workers and the aggressive creatures roaming the woods. With the Stormwind military stretched thin, guards like Thomas must rely heavily on passing adventurers to maintain order and carry messages back to central command.",["t"]="On the Eastern Border"},{["b"]="The eastern edges of Elwynn face persistent pressures. Aggressive bears and prowlers stalk the treeline, threatening lumberjacks and travelers, while strange murloc tribes have established camps along the waterways. Thomas tracks the movements of these aquatic predators and issues bounties to cull their numbers. Worse still, scouting patrols along the river occasionally vanish without a trace, leaving Thomas to piece together the fate of his fellow guards amidst rising regional instability.",["t"]="Frontier Troubles"}}}}}
t["npc:gunther-arcanus"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,371,20.392.0,21.596.0,17.549.1,23.229.0,73.258.0,42.272.0,38.213.0,31.216.1,22.198.1",["h"]="737437",["n"]="Gunther Arcanos",["s"]="Gunther Arcanos. Gunther Arcanos es un nigromante excepcionalmente poderoso que mora en una isla aislada en el Lago Aguasclaras. Asesinado durante la Tercera Guerra y levantado en la no-muerte, logró romper el control mental del Rey Exánime completamente por su cuenta. Creyendo durante mucho tiempo que era el único no-muerto con libre albedrío, defendió su retiro frente a cualquier intruso hasta que fue descubierto por los Renegados. Antes de la caída de Lordaeron, Gunther era un prometedor aprendiz entre el Kirin Tor en Dalaran. Junto a sus amigos cercanos Bethor Duroyelo y Thule Corvozarpa, estudió las artes arcanas, adentrándose en secreto en la nigromancia a pesar de las estrictas prohibiciones del Kirin Tor contra la magia oscura. Para conmemorar su hermandad, el trío unió una vez sus varitas de aprendiz en una sola reliquia.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,1,1},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="Trained in Dalaran, Gunther represents the Kirin Tor wizards who covertly dabbled in forbidden necromantic spells before the Scourge invaded Lordaeron.",["class:Warlock"]="Gunther's commanding grasp of dark arts and reanimation demonstrates how far forbidden scholarship could flourish outside the watchful eyes of Dalaran's leadership.",["race:Undead"]="Gunther's self-liberation makes him an anomaly among the Forsaken, proving that intense arcane training and iron will alone could sometimes shatter the Lich King's mental dominion."},["faq"]={{["a"]="He is a former wizard of the Kirin Tor from Dalaran who perished during the Third War. Raised into undeath, he broke free of the Lich King's domination on his own and retreated to an island in Brightwater Lake in Tirisfal Glades.",["al"]={"who is gunther","gunther lore","gunther arcanus story"},["q"]="Who is Gunther Arcanus?"},{["a"]="While traditional liches transfer their spirits into phylacteries and generate monstrous, floating skeletal forms, Gunther achieved his lich-like necromantic status without abandoning his original reanimated corpse, preserving his physical mortal appearance.",["al"]={"why does gunther look human","gunther not a skeleton","why is gunther a lich"},["q"]="Why does Gunther look like a regular Forsaken instead of a skeletal lich?"},{["a"]="After breaking the Lich King's mental control, Gunther believed he was the only undead in existence with free will. Assuming all other walking dead were still mindless slaves of the Scourge, he secluded himself and ordered his minions to strike down anyone who approached.",["al"]={"why is gunther alone","gunther island isolation","why does gunther hide"},["q"]="Why was Gunther living alone on an island?"},{["a"]="They were classmates and close friends in Dalaran studying under the Kirin Tor, along with a third mage named Thule Ravenclaw. The three friends even wove their apprentice wands together as a symbol of their bond.",["al"]={"bethor and gunther","how does gunther know bethor","bethor iceshard history"},["q"]="How does Gunther know Bethor Iceshard?"},{["a"]="Yes. Once adventurers return his enchanted spellbook and execute the local Scourge agent Lillith Nefara to prove their independence from the Lich King, Gunther pledges his allegiance to Bethor and the Forsaken cause.",["al"]={"does gunther join horde","gunther faction","is gunther forsaken"},["q"]="Does Gunther join the Forsaken?"},{["a"]="Lillith Nefara is an agent of the Scourge stationed in Tirisfal Glades. Gunther requires her death as proof that the adventurer truly serves an enemy of the Lich King rather than the Scourge itself.",["al"]={"lillith nefara","nefara","gunther target"},["q"]="Who is Lillith Nefara?"}},["kw"]={"arcanus","bethor","brightwater","dalaran","gunther","iceshard","kirin tor","lich","necromancer","thule","tirisfal"},["n"]="Gunther Arcanus",["s"]="Gunther Arcanus is an exceptionally powerful necromancer dwelling on an isolated island in Brightwater Lake. Slain during the Third War and raised into undeath, he managed to shatter the Lich King's mental grip entirely on his own. Long believing he was the sole undead possessing free will, he defended his retreat against all outsiders until discovered by the Forsaken.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the fall of Lordaeron, Gunther was a promising apprentice among the Kirin Tor in Dalaran. Alongside close friends Bethor Iceshard and Thule Ravenclaw, he studied the arcane arts, secretly delving into necromancy despite the Kirin Tor's strict prohibitions against dark magic. To commemorate their brotherhood, the trio once bound their apprentice wands together into a single heirloom.",["t"]="A Student of Dalaran"},{["b"]="When the Scourge swept across the north during the Third War, Gunther perished to the Plague of Undeath and was raised into servitude. Unlike most who required the Lich King's power to weaken or Lady Sylvanas to break their chains, Gunther's raw arcane mastery and sheer willpower allowed him to shake off the Lich King's mental domination entirely by himself. Convinced that every other walking corpse remained a mindless thrall of the Scourge, he retreated to an island in Tirisfal Glades, surrounding himself with shambling guardians and cutting off all contact with the living and dead alike.",["t"]="Breaking the Shackles"},{["b"]="Seeking powerful allies against the Scourge, the Forsaken sent emissaries to claim the mysterious necromancer's spellbook. Upon examining the arcane tome in the Undercity, Bethor Iceshard recognized the unique handwriting of his long-lost peer. By enchanting the returned grimoire and demanding the destruction of local Scourge commanders, Gunther finally realized he was not alone in his freedom. Convinced that Sylvanas's faction represents a true rebellion against the Scourge, he has forged a pact with his former schoolmate to aid the Forsaken.",["t"]="The Prodigal Lich"}}}}}
t["npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="21,348,29.489.0,19.409.0,29.212.0,39.134.0,43.248.0,32.196.0,52.234.0,24.167.0",["h"]="9e6415",["n"]="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",["s"]="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde. Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde es una elfa de la noche que reside en el puerto costero de Auberdine. Apostada a lo largo de la brumosa costa de Costa Oscura, vigila las mareas y encarga a los viajeros que investiguen los extraños restos que llegan a la orilla. Su preocupación se centra en las misteriosas criaturas marinas y las enormes tortugas cuyos cadáveres han comenzado a abarrotar las playas del norte. Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde tiene su hogar en Auberdine, el bullicioso refugio costero de Costa Oscura. Mientras muchos en la villa se preocupan por el bosque o por el transporte marítimo a través de Mar de la Bruma, Gwennyth mantiene la mirada fija en el litoral. Últimamente las mareas han tomado un cariz sombrío, arrastrando los restos de colosales seres marinos hasta la orilla. Para comprender lo que ocurre en las aguas mar adentro, confía en aventureros dispuestos a recorrer las arenas, recuperar muestras óseas y traer respuestas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Druids committed to preserving Kalimdor's natural harmony will find Gwennyth's reports of stranded marine life an alarming indicator of disturbance within the coastal ecosystem.",["faction:Alliance"]="Auberdine serves as the Alliance's primary coastal port in northern Kalimdor; keeping its waterways and beaches safe from hidden threats is vital to all allied races venturing through.",["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, the unnatural death of great sea beasts off the shores of Darkshore is a troubling sign of imbalance in their ancestral lands, making Gwennyth's beachside watch especially urgent."},["faq"]={{["a"]="She is a night elf inhabitant of Auberdine in Darkshore who studies the recent ecological disturbances along the shoreline. She enlists travelers to survey the beach and investigate strange wash-ups from the sea.",["al"]={"who is gwennyth","gwennyth auberdine","gwennyth lore"},["q"]="Who is Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde?"},{["a"]="She can be found in the coastal settlement of Auberdine, situated near the beach and docks along the mist-shrouded coast of Darkshore.",["al"]={"where is gwennyth","gwennyth location","find gwennyth"},["q"]="Where can I find Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde?"},{["a"]="The sudden deaths and beachings of massive sea turtles and mysterious marine behemoths point to an imbalance or unseen predator in the waters off Darkshore. Gwennyth seeks to understand the cause by examining remains recovered from along the coast.",["al"]={"why beached turtles","why does she want bones","washed ashore quest"},["q"]="Why is she interested in beached creatures?"},{["a"]="She sends adventurers out on 'Washed Ashore' and serves as the turn-in point for various discoveries related to the beached sea creatures and beached sea turtles found along Darkshore's coastline.",["al"]={"gwennyth quests","what does she give"},["q"]="What quests does Gwennyth offer?"},{["a"]="Neither. She is a Priestess of the Moon serving the Sisters of Elune in Auberdine rather than a Cenarion druid or Sentinel commander, yet she shares her kin's deep concern for the health and balance of Darkshore's natural environment.",["al"]={"gwennyth faction","is gwennyth a druid"},["q"]="Is she part of the Cenarion Circle or the Sentinels?"},{["a"]="While fitting the rhythmic naming style of the kaldorei, her unusual surname 'Bly'Leggonde' is an anagram of 'Leggy Blonde', a playful touch from the world's creators.",["al"]={"bly leggonde meaning","gwennyth name easter egg"},["q"]="What does her name mean?"}},["kw"]={"auberdine","beached sea creature","beached sea turtle","blyleggonde","darkshore","gwennyth","kaldorei","veiled sea","washed ashore"},["n"]="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",["s"]="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde is a night elf residing in the coastal port of Auberdine. Stationed along the misty Darkshore coast, she watches the tides and directs travelers to investigate the strange remains washing ashore. Her concerns center on the mysterious sea creatures and massive turtles whose carcasses have begun littering the northern beaches.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde makes her home in Auberdine, the bustling seaside haven of Darkshore. While many in town concern themselves with the forest or shipping across the Veiled Sea, Gwennyth keeps her gaze firmly on the coastline. The tides have recently turned grim, depositing the remains of colossal marine life onto the surf. To understand what is happening in the waters offshore, she relies on willing adventurers to scour the sands, retrieve skeletal samples, and bring back answers.",["t"]="Watcher of the Shifting Sands"},{["b"]="The beaches north and south of Auberdine have seen an alarming influx of beached sea creatures and ancient sea turtles. Rather than letting their deaths go unnoticed, Gwennyth tasks travelers with inspecting these fallen titans. By studying the bones and discovering what drove these beasts ashore or took their lives, she hopes to piece together the hidden perils lurking off the shores of northern Kalimdor.",["t"]="The Stranded Giants"}}}}}
t["npc:hamhock"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="7,255,19.324.0,13.366.0,15.192.0,49.243.0,42.197.0,44.185.0,48.179.0,37.209.0",["h"]="fd7f37",["n"]="Hamhock",["s"]="Hamhock. Hamhock es un descomunal ogro de dos cabezas recluido en las profundidades de las Mazmorras de Ventormenta. Encerrado bajo la capital junto a curtidos insurgentes y degolladores Defias, se erige como un recluso particularmente brutal e inesperado en medio del motín carcelario. Las Mazmorras de Ventormenta se construyeron para albergar a ladronzuelos, asesinos y disidentes políticos, lo que convierte a un imponente ogro de dos cabezas en una visión imponente entre las celdas. Cuando los prisioneros se alzaron y tomaron el control de las instalaciones, Hamhock permaneció atrincherado en el caos, aplastando a cualquiera lo bastante insensato como para adentrarse en su bloque de celdas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warrior"]="Subduing Hamhock requires meeting raw, hulking strength head-on within the tight confines of the prison hallways.",["faction:Alliance"]="Finding a two-headed ogre unrestrained directly beneath the capital's streets underscores just how catastrophically the city guards have lost control of the Stockade."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Hamhock is an elite two-headed ogre prisoner held within the Stormwind Stockade. Amid the uprising led by the Defias convicts, he acts as a dangerous obstacle deep inside the prison corridors.",["al"]={"hamhock","who is the ogre in stockade","ogre boss stockade"},["q"]="Who is Hamhock?"},{["a"]="Official records do not detail his capture, but he is widely thought to either be a captured brute from the Splinter Fist clan inhabiting Duskwood or a hired enforcer employed by the Defias Brotherhood who was caught during illicit operations.",["al"]={"why is hamhock in jail","how did hamhock get captured","why is there an ogre in stockades"},["q"]="How did an ogre end up in the Stormwind Stockade?"},{["a"]="While the entire facility has fallen into rebellion under Defias ringleaders, it is unclear whether Hamhock truly coordinates with them or simply revels in the unbridled mayhem of the broken cells.",["al"]={"is hamhock defias","hamhock defias brotherhood","does hamhock work for bazil"},["q"]="Is Hamhock allied with the Defias rioters?"},{["a"]="Many believe he originated from the Vul'Gol Ogre Mound in Duskwood, which would place him among the Splinter Fist clan led by Zzarc'Vul prior to being captured and brought to Stormwind.",["al"]={"is hamhock splinter fist","hamhock vulgol","vul'gol ogres stockade"},["q"]="Is Hamhock related to the ogres in Duskwood?"},{["a"]="No official bounties or city warrants are offered specifically for Hamhock's head. He is an incidental menace whom adventurers encounter while clearing out the rioting stronghold.",["al"]={"hamhock quest","is there a quest for hamhock","hamhock bounty"},["q"]="Is Hamhock tied to any specific bounty or quest?"},{["a"]="Two-headed ogres possess distinct personalities between their heads and are often more cunning or magically adept than their single-headed kin, making Hamhock exceptionally dangerous to standard prison guards.",["al"]={"two headed ogre lore","why two heads"},["q"]="Why are two-headed ogres significant?"}},["kw"]={"duskwood","hamhock","ogre","prison","splinter fist","stockade","stormwind","two-headed"},["n"]="Hamhock",["s"]="Hamhock is a massive two-headed ogre confined within the depths of the Stormwind Stockade. Locked away beneath the capital alongside hardened Defias insurgents and cutthroats, he looms as a particularly brutal and unexpected inmate amidst the prison riot.",["sec"]={{["b"]="The Stormwind Stockade was built to hold petty thieves, murderers, and political dissidents, making a towering two-headed ogre an imposing sight among the cells. When the prisoners rose up and took control of the facility, Hamhock remained entrenched in the chaos, crushing anyone foolish enough to intrude on his cellblock.",["t"]="A Brute Behind Bars"},{["b"]="Stormwind authorities keep few public records regarding how Hamhock was captured. Popular speculation among guards and city residents suggests he may have been dragged north from the Splinter Fist clan at Duskwood's Vul'Gol Ogre Mound. Others suspect he was recruited into the Defias Brotherhood as mercenary muscle before falling into the custody of the city watch.",["t"]="Murky Origins"}}}}}
t["npc:herod"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="5,373,26.452.0,22.488.0,13.228.0,23.200.0,35.239.0,38.254.0,36.201.1,30.210.0",["h"]="bb3b37",["n"]="Herod",["s"]="Herod. Herod es un renombrado adalid y bersérker de la Cruzada Escarlata que comanda la Armería dentro del Monasterio Escarlata. Conocido por su feroz destreza marcial y su inquebrantable celo, entrena a los reclutas en el brutal combate cuerpo a cuerpo necesario para librar una guerra santa. Tanto los disidentes de la Alianza como los gobernantes de la Horda en Entrañas buscan su muerte para debilitar el núcleo militar de la Cruzada. Dentro de las salas fortificadas de la Armería del Monasterio Escarlata, Herod representa la personificación de la agresividad marcial de la Cruzada. A diferencia de los taumaturgos y paladines que canalizan magia sagrada en la Catedral, Herod confía en un poder físico puro y sanguinario. Ataviado con malla y blandiendo una descomunal hacha de dos manos, entrena personalmente a cohortes de aprendices escarlata, inculcándoles una furiosa devoción por exterminar a cualquiera que no esté aliado con su fanática causa.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,1,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warrior"]="Herod is a prime example of an enraged warrior whose furious whirlwind strikes and reckless aggression make him a feared martial paragon among the Scarlet Crusade's recruits.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance heroes who answer Raleigh the Devout's plea can witness firsthand how the once-noble defenders of Lordaeron have fallen into deranged, fanatical bloodlust under leaders like Herod.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde and the Forsaken in particular, eliminating Herod directly fulfills Varimathras's orders to break the leadership threatening the borders of Tirisfal Glades."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Herod is an elite human warrior and commander of the Armory in the Scarlet Monastery. He serves as one of the four principal leaders of the Monastery, responsible for outfitting and drilling the Crusade's zealous melee fighters.",["al"]={"herod lore","who is herod","herod scarlet monastery"},["q"]="Who is Herod?"},{["a"]="Herod can be found at the heart of the Armory wing in the Scarlet Monastery, situated in northeastern Tirisfal Glades. He awaits challengers in a central training ring surrounded by viewing galleries.",["al"]={"where is herod","herod location","find herod"},["q"]="Where is Herod located?"},{["a"]="The dreadlord Varimathras, acting on behalf of the Forsaken in the Undercity, seeks the elimination of the Monastery's key commanders—including Herod—to eradicate the Crusade's lingering threat right on the Forsaken capital's doorstep.",["al"]={"varimathras herod quest","why horde kill herod","into the scarlet monastery"},["q"]="Why does the Horde want Herod dead?"},{["a"]="Raleigh the Devout, a former member of the Scarlet Crusade stationed in Hillsbrad Foothills, recognizes that the order has descended into fanatical zealotry. He asks Alliance champions to purge Herod to strip the Crusade of its brutal warrior leadership.",["al"]={"in the name of the light","raleigh the devout herod","why alliance kill herod"},["q"]="Why does the Alliance want Herod dead?"},{["a"]="Upon Herod's defeat, a mob of young Scarlet Trainees surges out from the surrounding barracks into the ring to avenge their master, illustrating the sheer depth of devotion he fostered in his students.",["al"]={"scarlet trainees","herod trainee rush","herod death event"},["q"]="What happens when Herod is defeated?"},{["a"]="Herod is a berserker and warrior rather than a traditional holy paladin. He uses vicious charges and sweeping whirlwind strikes to pulverize foes, relying on sheer physical frenzy over spells of the Holy Light.",["al"]={"herod fighting style","is herod a paladin"},["q"]="What kind of fighter is Herod?"}},["kw"]={"armory","berserker","herod","raleigh the devout","ravager","scarlet crusade","scarlet monastery","varimathras"},["n"]="Herod",["s"]="Herod is a renowned champion and berserker of the Scarlet Crusade, commanding the Armory within the Scarlet Monastery. Known for his ferocious martial prowess and unyielding zeal, he trains recruits in the brutal melee combat needed to wage holy war. His death is sought by both Alliance dissidents and the Horde's rulers in Undercity to weaken the Crusade's military core.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Within the fortified halls of the Scarlet Monastery's Armory, Herod stands as the embodiment of the Crusade's martial aggression. Unlike the spellcasters and paladins who channel holy magic in the Cathedral, Herod relies on raw, bloodthirsty physical power. Clad in mail and wielding a massive two-handed axe, he personally trains cohorts of Scarlet Trainees, instilling a furious devotion to exterminating anyone not allied with their fanatical cause.",["t"]="The Champion of the Armory"},{["b"]="Because Herod oversees the armaments and martial training of the Crusade's front-line warriors, taking him down is essential for anyone seeking to dismantle the order. Raleigh the Devout, an ex-Crusader disillusioned with the order's madness residing in Southshore, calls for Herod's demise to shatter their military leadership. Across Lordaeron, the dreadlord Varimathras in the Undercity similarly seeks his execution to clear out a dangerous human bastion bordering Forsaken territory.",["t"]="A High-Priority Target"}}}}}
t["npc:high-executor-darthalia"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="23,385,24.440.0,21.364.0,31.235.0,29.129.0,29.208.0,46.198.0,51.216.0,50.207.0",["h"]="cfbd72",["n"]="Suma Ejecutora Darthalia",["s"]="Suma Ejecutora Darthalia. La Suma Ejecutora Darthalia es una comandante militar renegada de alto rango destinada en Molino Tarren, en las Laderas de Trabalomas. Actuando bajo la autoridad directa de Lady Sylvanas Brisaveloz y Varimathras, dirige las operaciones de los Renegados contra el bastión humano de Costasur y los bandidos locales de la Hermandad. Su liderazgo es fundamental para asegurar el flanco sur de la Horda en Lordaeron. Operando desde Molino Tarren, la Suma Ejecutora Darthalia ejerce como comandante operacional de las fuerzas de los Renegados en todas las Laderas de Trabalomas. Su principal preocupación estratégica es detener la expansión de la resistencia humana, mantener contenidas a las fuerzas de la Alianza en Costasur y dar caza a los forajidos de la Hermandad que infestan la campiña circundante. Cada ofensiva hacia el sur de Trabalomas pasa directamente por su mando.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="To the humans of Southshore and their allies, Darthalia is the ruthless architect behind the relentless assaults threatening their last foothold in Lordaeron.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde adventurers report to Darthalia to check Alliance aggression and hold the contested frontier of Hillsbrad Foothills.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, Darthalia represents the iron will of the Undercity, ensuring that Lordaeron remains firmly in the hands of the free-willed undead."},["faq"]={{["a"]="High Executor Darthalia is a Forsaken military leader stationed in Hillsbrad Foothills. She is responsible for directing Horde and Forsaken military efforts against the human town of Southshore and eliminating hostile regional threats.",["al"]={"who is darthalia","darthalia identity","executor darthalia"},["q"]="Who is High Executor Darthalia?"},{["a"]="She commands Forsaken forces from Tarren Mill, organizing troops and coordinating strikes across the central region of Lordaeron.",["al"]={"darthalia location","where is darthalia","executor darthalia map"},["q"]="Where can Darthalia be found?"},{["a"]="Darthalia operates under the direct military hierarchy of the Undercity, answering to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the dreadlord Varimathras as they coordinate the defense and expansion of Forsaken territory.",["al"]={"darthalia boss","darthalia faction","who commands darthalia"},["q"]="Who does Darthalia answer to?"},{["a"]="Darthalia tasks Horde champions with striking directly against human settlements, executing dangerous outlaws, and hunting down members of the Syndicate operating throughout the Hillsbrad Foothills.",["al"]={"darthalia quests","quests from darthalia","what does darthalia want"},["q"]="What tasks does Darthalia give to adventurers?"},{["a"]="Southshore represents the primary Alliance military foothold in Lordaeron. Darthalia's mission is to suppress the human presence, protect Tarren Mill, and prevent the Alliance from pushing north toward the Undercity.",["al"]={"why attack southshore","southshore war","hillsbrad conflict"},["q"]="Why is Darthalia fighting the humans of Southshore?"},{["a"]="As a High Executor, Darthalia holds one of the highest field-grade ranks within the Forsaken military hierarchy, granting her operational command over regional forces, outposts, and war strategy in the zone.",["al"]={"high executor rank","darthalia title"},["q"]="What is Darthalia's rank in the Forsaken military?"}},["kw"]={"darthalia","high executor","hillsbrad","hillsbrad foothills","southshore","sylvanas","syndicate","tarren mill","varimathras"},["n"]="High Executor Darthalia",["s"]="High Executor Darthalia is a high-ranking Forsaken military commander stationed at Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Acting under the direct authority of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and Varimathras, she directs Forsaken operations against the human stronghold of Southshore and local Syndicate brigands. Her leadership is central to securing the Horde's southern flank in Lordaeron.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Operating out of Tarren Mill, High Executor Darthalia serves as the operational commander for Forsaken forces throughout the Hillsbrad Foothills. Her primary strategic concern is halting the expansion of human resistance, keeping the Alliance forces in Southshore contained, and hunting down the lawless Syndicate rogues infesting the surrounding countryside. Every offensive push into southern Hillsbrad flows directly through her command.",["t"]="Commander of Tarren Mill"},{["b"]="Under direct orders originating from the Undercity's high leadership—the Banshee Queen and her dreadlord lieutenant, Varimathras—Darthalia oversees the relentless attrition war across Hillsbrad. She coordinates scouting missions, targeted strikes against human leadership, and bounties on dangerous outlaws who threaten the Forsaken hold on northern Lordaeron.",["t"]="The War for Hillsbrad"}}}}}
t["npc:high-executor-hadrec"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="20,377,26.464.0,20.432.0,17.369.1,28.201.0,40.130.0,48.229.0,60.208.0,40.233.0,47.226.0",["h"]="6f7253",["n"]="Sumo Ejecutor Hadrec",["s"]="Sumo Ejecutor Hadrec. El Sumo Ejecutor Hadrec es el comandante militar de la guarnición de los Renegados apostada en El Sepulcro, en el Bosque de Argénteos. Desde esta cripta central, supervisa la defensa contra las amenazas regionales, incluidos los gnolls del clan Putrepellejo, e investiga la desaparición de exploradores por toda la zona. Ejerce como el oficial principal que dirige las operaciones de la Horda en todo Argénteos. Apostado en la penumbra de El Sepulcro, el Sumo Ejecutor Hadrec dirige las operaciones militares de los Renegados en el Bosque de Argénteos. Mientras que los Claros de Tirisfal están firmemente asegurados por las fuerzas de la Dama Oscura, Argénteos sigue plagado de peligros, rodeado de magos hostiles de Dalaran, feroces huargen y gnolls invasores. Hadrec carga con la sombría responsabilidad de consolidar el territorio de los Renegados y erradicar todo lo que desafíe la autoridad de Entrañas al sur de la capital.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="Hadrec relies heavily on the Deathstalkers for intelligence, frequently employing stealthy operatives to recover missing comrades and gather enemy ichor and documents.",["faction:Horde"]="Allies of the Forsaken arriving from Kalimdor report to Hadrec to aid in stabilizing Silverpine, learning firsthand how tenuous the Horde's foothold in northern Lordaeron remains.",["race:Undead"]="For Forsaken traveling south from Deathknell, Hadrec represents the voice of the Undercity's high command, turning newborn undead into organized defenders of Lordaeron."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Hadrec is a Forsaken military officer holding the rank of High Executor. He commands the garrison based at the Sepulcher, making him the supreme Forsaken authority over operations in Silverpine Forest.",["al"]={"hadrec lore","who is hadrec","sepulcher commander"},["q"]="Who is High Executor Hadrec?"},{["a"]="He is located inside the Sepulcher, the Forsaken settlement situated in central Silverpine Forest along the main north-south road.",["al"]={"hadrec location","where is hadrec","find hadrec"},["q"]="Where can High Executor Hadrec be found?"},{["a"]="Hadrec directs soldiers and adventurers against the Rot Hide gnolls that plague the Dead Fields and Fenris Isle. He also oversees missions to locate missing Deathstalker spies and uncover what is unfolding inside Shadowfang Keep.",["al"]={"hadrec quests","what does hadrec do","silverpine missions"},["q"]="What threats does Hadrec direct players against?"},{["a"]="A High Executor is a high-ranking field commander in the Forsaken military, entrusted with full strategic oversight of an entire regional outpost or front line under the authority of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner.",["al"]={"forsaken high executor","high executor rank","hadrec rank"},["q"]="What does a High Executor do in Forsaken military structure?"},{["a"]="Fenris Isle has become the primary den of the Rot Hide gnolls. To secure Lake Lordamere and the surrounding waterways for Forsaken supply lines, Hadrec coordinates reconnaissance and an eventual assault to break the gnoll leadership.",["al"]={"fenris isle hadrec","why assault fenris isle","rot hide fenris"},["q"]="Why is Hadrec interested in Fenris Isle?"},{["a"]="Hadrec coordinates with the Deathstalkers, the Forsaken espionage order. When scouts sent toward Shadowfang Keep fail to report back, Hadrec commissions trusted agents to investigate the keep and uncover what happened to them.",["al"]={"shadowfang keep hadrec","hadrec arugal","deathstalkers in shadowfang"},["q"]="What is Hadrec's connection to Shadowfang Keep?"}},["kw"]={"deathstalker","fenris isle","hadrec","high executor","rot hide","sepulcher","shadowfang","silverpine"},["n"]="High Executor Hadrec",["s"]="High Executor Hadrec is the military commander of the Forsaken garrison stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. From this central crypt, he oversees defense against regional threats including the gnolls of the Rot Hide clan and investigates the disappearance of scouts across the zone. He serves as the primary officer directing Horde operations throughout Silverpine.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Stationed within the gloom of the Sepulcher, High Executor Hadrec directs Forsaken military operations across Silverpine Forest. While Tirisfal Glades is firmly secured by the Dark Lady's forces, Silverpine remains fraught with peril, bordered by hostile Dalaran mages, feral worgen, and encroaching gnolls. Hadrec bears the grim responsibility of consolidating Forsaken territory and stamping out anything that challenges Undercity authority south of the capital.",["t"]="Commander at the Sepulcher"},{["b"]="Much of Hadrec's immediate concern revolves around the Rot Hide gnolls and Fenris Isle. These undead-tainted beasts have infested the Dead Fields and the shores of Lake Lordamere, posing an unpredictable and vicious threat to Forsaken patrols. Hadrec dispatches agents to scour the decrepit ferries and rotting farmsteads for clues, determine what empowers the beasts, and prepare an outright strike against their island stronghold.",["t"]="The Rot Hide Scourge"},{["b"]="Beyond the gnoll infestation, Hadrec closely monitors intelligence gathered by the Deathstalkers, the Forsaken's secretive rogue intelligence arm. When covert operatives disappear near the eerie spires of Shadowfang Keep, Hadrec tasks adventurers with discovering their fate, ensuring the Dark Lady remains informed of the shadowy archmage Arugal and his cursed worgen.",["t"]="Eye on Shadowfang"}}}}}
t["npc:high-priestess-laurena"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="22,297,22.515.0,20.585.0,40.123.0,39.227.0,45.214.0,43.166.0,48.338.0,42.203.0",["h"]="864c89",["n"]="Suma Sacerdotisa Laurena",["s"]="Suma Sacerdotisa Laurena. La Suma Sacerdotisa Laurena es una respetada instructora de sacerdotes humana situada detrás del gran altar dentro de la Catedral de la Luz, en la Ciudad de Ventormenta. Tras haber escapado de la destrucción de Lordaeron como refugiada durante la Tercera Guerra, ahora instruye a los sacerdotes novatos de la Alianza en la devoción espiritual y las protecciones arcanas. Antes de ocupar su puesto en las imponentes salas de la Catedral de la Luz, Laurena vivía en el reino norteño de Lordaeron. Cuando la Plaga arrasó la región durante la Tercera Guerra, ella y toda su familia tuvieron la suerte de sobrevivir y huir hacia el sur, llegando a la Ciudad de Ventormenta como refugiados desplazados. A pesar del inmenso dolor y el caos que destruyeron su tierra natal, Laurena se mantuvo firme en su devoción y con el tiempo ascendió hasta convertirse en Suma Sacerdotisa al servicio de la Iglesia de la Luz Sagrada.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Priest"]="High Priestess Laurena acts as one of Stormwind's primary priest mentors, guiding human acolytes through sacred trials, blessing them with Desperate Prayer, and teaching methods to disrupt enemy spellcasters.",["faction:Alliance"]="From within the Cathedral of Light, Laurena helps strengthen the spiritual backbone of the Alliance, ensuring its champions can withstand dark magic and undead horrors.",["race:Human"]="Like many humans in Stormwind, Laurena carries the sorrow of the fallen northern realm of Lordaeron, having rebuilt her life as a spiritual pillar for fellow survivors."},["faq"]={{["a"]="She stands behind the main altar inside the Cathedral of Light, which is located in Cathedral Square within Stormwind City.",["al"]={"laurena location","where is priestess laurena","find laurena"},["q"]="Where can I find High Priestess Laurena?"},{["a"]="Laurena is a priest trainer. She provides foundational instruction to human priests and teaches specialized racial prayers such as Desperate Prayer, as well as wards like Arcane Feedback to protect against hostile spellcasters.",["al"]={"laurena spells","priest trainer laurena","what does laurena teach"},["q"]="What does High Priestess Laurena teach?"},{["a"]="Laurena originally lived in the kingdom of Lordaeron. During the Third War, her family managed to escape the horrors of the Scourge and fled to Stormwind City as refugees, where she continued her religious calling.",["al"]={"laurena backstory","is laurena from stormwind","laurena lordaeron"},["q"]="Where did Laurena come from before Stormwind?"},{["a"]="Yes. Archbishop Benedictus is the spiritual leader of the Church of the Holy Light and presides over the Cathedral of Light, where Laurena serves as a High Priestess.",["al"]={"laurena and benedictus","who is laurena's boss","benedictus laurena"},["q"]="Does she serve under Archbishop Benedictus?"},{["a"]="Different cultures and races within the Alliance commune with the divine in unique ways. Once Laurena has taught her students the foundational prayers of the Holy Light, she sends them to master priests of other disciplines—such as dwarven masters in Ironforge or night elf priestesses in Darnassus—to expand their spiritual horizons.",["al"]={"laurena sends me away","a lack of fear quest","elunes grace quest"},["q"]="Why does she direct me to other priest trainers?"},{["a"]="Remarkably, her immediate family survived the fall of Lordaeron. They were among the fortunate refugees who managed to escape the Scourge intact and make the long voyage south to the safety of Stormwind.",["al"]={"laurena family dead","what happened to laurena family"},["q"]="Did Laurena lose her family to the undead?"}},["kw"]={"arcane feedback","benedictus","cathedral of light","desperate prayer","high priestess","holy light","laurena","lordaeron","priest trainer","stormwind"},["n"]="High Priestess Laurena",["s"]="High Priestess Laurena is a respected human priest trainer stationed behind the grand altar within Stormwind City's Cathedral of Light. Having escaped the destruction of Lordaeron as a refugee during the Third War, she now instructs budding Alliance priests in spiritual devotion and arcane wards.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before taking her post within the towering halls of the Cathedral of Light, Laurena dwelt in the northern kingdom of Lordaeron. When the Scourge swept across the land during the Third War, she and her entire family were fortunate enough to survive and flee southward, arriving in Stormwind City as displaced refugees. Despite the immense grief and chaos that shattered her homeland, Laurena remained steadfast in her devotion, eventually rising to become a High Priestess in service to the Church of the Holy Light.",["t"]="A Refugee of Lordaeron"},{["b"]="Positioned directly behind the central altar within the cathedral sanctuary, High Priestess Laurena dedicates herself to mentoring aspiring priests. When promising acolytes demonstrate sufficient dedication and piety, they are directed to her to deepen their studies. Laurena guides them in the invocation of sacred boons such as Desperate Prayer and instructs them in defensive arts, including spells designed to turn enemy arcane magic back against those who wield it. Once an initiate has learned all she can offer, she sends them onward to other master priests across the Alliance.",["t"]="Tending the Faithful"}}}}}
t["npc:houndmaster-loksey"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,355,21.443.0,14.441.0,38.160.0,51.205.0,34.214.0,40.167.0,55.170.0,38.165.0",["h"]="48d283",["n"]="Domador de jaurías Loksey",["s"]="Domador de jaurías Loksey. El Domador de jaurías Loksey es el oficial encargado de criar y adiestrar a los temibles perros de guerra de la Cruzada Escarlata. Destinado en las perreras del interior de la Armería del Monasterio Escarlata, dirige jaurías de sabuesos para dar caza a no-muertos, intrusos y supuestos herejes. Su disciplina despiadada ha hecho que las bestias del Monasterio sean infames en todos los Claros de Tirisfal. Entre los muros fuertemente fortificados del Monasterio Escarlata, el Domador de jaurías Loksey dirige el adiestramiento de feroces perros de rastreo y ataque. La Cruzada Escarlata confía en estos sabuesos entrenados para olfatear cadáveres corrompidos por la peste, descubrir infiltrados ocultos y perseguir a cualquier superviviente que huya de la ira de los fanáticos. Loksey ostenta una autoridad absoluta sobre el ala de las perreras de la Armería, asegurándose de que sus pupilos estén listos para despedazar a los intrusos miembro a miembro.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Hunter"]="Loksey exemplifies a brutal, aggressive approach to beast training, bending fierce hounds to obey zealotry rather than forging a bond of mutual respect.",["race:Undead"]="Forsaken intruders must beware Loksey's hounds, which are trained specifically to catch the scent of dead flesh and alert the Crusade's garrisons."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Houndmaster Loksey is located inside the Armory wing of the Scarlet Monastery in northeastern Tirisfal Glades, surrounded by his attack dogs within the kennels.",["al"]={"loksey location","where is loksey","houndmaster loksey location"},["q"]="Where can Houndmaster Loksey be found?"},{["a"]="He is the chief animal handler and houndmaster for the Scarlet Crusade at the Monastery, responsible for breeding, conditioning, and directing the war dogs used to sniff out undead and hunt down intruders.",["al"]={"what does loksey do","loksey job","houndmaster duty"},["q"]="What role does Loksey serve in the Scarlet Crusade?"},{["a"]="Huntsman Leopold is Loksey's brother. Leopold represents the Scarlet Crusade at Light's Hope Chapel and looks down on Loksey, claiming Loksey cannot properly manage his hounds or handle diplomatic responsibilities.",["al"]={"leopold loksey brother","who is leopold","loksey brother"},["q"]="Who is Huntsman Leopold to Loksey?"},{["a"]="The Crusade trains vicious hounds to track down the Scourge and Forsaken through scent, as well as to guard the Monastery's grounds and tear fleeing enemies to pieces.",["al"]={"why dogs","scarlet hounds purpose","crusade dogs"},["q"]="Why does the Scarlet Crusade use hounds?"},{["a"]="Yes, Loksey is recognized as one of the key commanding figures in the Scarlet Monastery's military structure, overseeing the critical kennel operations within the Armory.",["al"]={"is loksey a boss","loksey rank","how important is loksey"},["q"]="Is Loksey considered a leader of the Scarlet Monastery?"},{["a"]="Yes. Bred for aggression and conditioned by Loksey, the Monastery's war hounds are fierce predators capable of ripping an armored intruder limb from limb in moments.",["al"]={"are dogs strong","scarlet hounds danger","loksey pets"},["q"]="Are the hounds dangerous on their own?"}},["kw"]={"armory","houndmaster loksey","hounds","huntsman leopold","kennels","loksey","scarlet crusade","scarlet monastery"},["n"]="Houndmaster Loksey",["s"]="Houndmaster Loksey is the officer charged with breeding and training the fearsome war dogs of the Scarlet Crusade. Stationed in the kennels within the Scarlet Monastery's Armory, he directs packs of hounds to hunt down undead, intruders, and perceived heretics. His merciless discipline has made the Monastery's beasts infamous throughout Tirisfal Glades.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Within the heavily fortified walls of the Scarlet Monastery, Houndmaster Loksey commands the training of vicious tracking and attack dogs. The Scarlet Crusade relies on these trained hounds to sniff out plague-tainted corpses, uncover hidden infiltrators, and run down any survivors fleeing the zealots' wrath. Loksey holds absolute authority over the Armory's kennel wing, ensuring his charges are primed to tear intruders apart limb by limb.",["t"]="Master of the Kennels"},{["b"]="Loksey is not the only beast handler in his family serving the cause. His brother, Huntsman Leopold, serves as the Scarlet Crusade's envoy to the Argent Dawn at Light's Hope Chapel. Leopold holds a low opinion of his brother, privately asserting that Loksey can barely manage his own hounds, let alone represent the order in high-stakes diplomacy. Despite Leopold's scorn, Loksey remains a key officer within the Monastery's inner hierarchy.",["t"]="Family Rivalry"}}}}}
t["npc:interrogator-vishas"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="19,348,30.526.0,27.533.1,39.184.0,38.249.0,22.210.0,31.236.0,30.139.0,40.206.0",["h"]="ebb32c",["n"]="Interrogador Vishas",["s"]="Interrogador Vishas. El Interrogador James Vishas es el maestro del tormento de la Cruzada Escarlata, apostado en lo más profundo del Cementerio del Monasterio Escarlata. Célebre por su voz estridente y su crueldad absoluta, disfruta de una manera retorcida quebrando a los cautivos y poniendo a prueba los límites de la carne mortal. Pocos de los que entran en sus cámaras de tortura vuelven a salir con la mente o el cuerpo intactos. En el interior de las oscuras criptas y los camposantos del Monasterio Escarlata, el Interrogador Vishas se ocupa de los enemigos apresados por la Cruzada. Mientras los fanáticos del exterior desfilan con armaduras resplandecientes bajo estandartes de pureza, Vishas encarna la cruda realidad que se oculta tras su cruzada: un sadismo desenfrenado disfrazado de justa furia religiosa. Vishas no aborda el interrogatorio como una simple labor de inteligencia, sino como un preciado oficio, deleitándose con la agonía de los cautivos Renegados, los miembros de la Plaga capturados y cualquier viajero vivo con la mala fortuna de haber sido tachado de hereje.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Priest"]="Seeing Vishas invoke zealotry to sanctify horrific mutilation offers a chilling demonstration of how holy purpose can curdle into twisted madness.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance heroes who discover Vishas' work quickly realize that the Scarlet Crusade no longer distinguishes between Scourge monsters and innocent living travelers.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, Vishas embodies the hypocritical malice of the living zealots, torturing captured undead out of pure spite while claiming to serve the Holy Light."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Interrogator Vishas is located deep inside the Graveyard wing of the Scarlet Monastery, in Tirisfal Glades. He oversees a grim torture chamber lined with iron cages and bloodied racks.",["al"]={"vishas location","where is interrogator vishas","vishas room"},["q"]="Where can Interrogator Vishas be found?"},{["a"]="While the Scarlet Crusade justifies tormenting captives to root out Scourge corruption and extract information, Vishas personally delights in the pain he causes. He takes enormous personal pride in his cruelty, viewing torture as his artistic craft.",["al"]={"why is vishas torturing people","vishas motivation"},["q"]="Why does Vishas torture his prisoners?"},{["a"]="Vorrel Sengutz is a captive imprisoned and brutally tortured by Vishas inside the Monastery's Graveyard. Vishas subjected Vorrel to weeks of pain and stole his wedding band, intending it as a gift for his wife.",["al"]={"vorrel sengutz prisoner","who is the prisoner in the cage"},["q"]="Who is Vorrel Sengutz?"},{["a"]="His family lives far from the Monastery, at an unassuming cottage situated along the eastern bank of Lordamere Lake in the Alterac Mountains. His wife Nancy and Grandpa Vishas dwell there quietly, seemingly detached from his atrocities.",["al"]={"nancy vishas location","grandpa vishas","vishas family house"},["q"]="Where does Vishas' family live?"},{["a"]="The Scarlet Crusade regards the undead as enemies. Among Vishas's prisoners is the Forsaken Vorrel Sengutz, whom he has tortured for weeks.",["al"]={"vishas prisoners","who does vishas torture","vishas captive vorrel"},["q"]="Who does Vishas hold prisoner?"},{["a"]="Vishas is infamous among those who face him for his grating, high-pitched voice, cackling laughter, and disturbing excitement whenever an opportunity presents itself to rip secrets from an unwilling victim.",["al"]={"vishas voice","vishas personality"},["q"]="What is Vishas' voice and demeanor like?"}},["kw"]={"graveyard","interrogator vishas","james vishas","lordamere lake","nancy vishas","scarlet monastery","torture","vorrel sengutz"},["n"]="Interrogator Vishas",["s"]="Interrogator James Vishas is the Scarlet Crusade's master of torment, stationed deep within the Scarlet Monastery's Graveyard wing. Infamous for his shrill voice and sheer cruelty, he takes twisted pleasure in breaking captives and testing the limits of mortal flesh. Few who enter his torture chambers ever leave with their minds or bodies intact.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Within the dark crypts and burial grounds of the Scarlet Monastery, Interrogator Vishas tends to the Crusade's captive enemies. While the zealots outside march in gleaming armor under banners of purity, Vishas represents the grim reality behind their crusade: unbridled sadism cloaked in religious righteous fury. He approaches interrogation not merely as an intelligence duty, but as a prized craft, reveling in the agony of Forsaken captives, captured Scourge, and any living travelers unlucky enough to be branded heretics.",["t"]="The Grand Inquisitor's Scalpel"},{["b"]="Behind the bloody aprons and screams of the torture chamber, Vishas leads a bizarrely domestic double life. Outside the monastery walls, his family—including his wife, Nancy Vishas, and his elder relative Grandpa Vishas—resides peacefully in an isolated cottage on the eastern shores of Lordamere Lake in the Alterac Mountains. Vishas even carries gruesome tokens from his victims back into his personal life, having stripped a captive Forsaken named Vorrel Sengutz of his cherished wedding ring to present it as a gift to Nancy.",["t"]="A Life of Quiet Domesticity"}}}}}
t["npc:islen-waterseer"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,354,25.454.0,27.423.0,22.406.0,23.251.0,33.258.0,33.151.0,38.240.0,37.207.0,49.206.0",["h"]="b7ae72",["n"]="Islen Vident'aqua",["s"]="Islen Vident'aqua. Islen Vident'aqua es una respetada chamán tauren que mora junto a una tranquila cabaña de pesca en el Escalón de la Marea, con vistas al mar oriental de Los Baldíos. Al poseer una íntima comunión con los espíritus del agua, guía a los iniciados en las pruebas necesarias para sintonizar con el elemento. Los chamanes novatos de toda la Horda buscan su sabiduría para obtener su Tótem de agua. Lejos de los bulliciosos cruces de caminos y campamentos de Los Baldíos, Islen Vident'aqua vive a lo largo de la escarpada costa conocida como el Escalón de la Marea. Aquí, donde las áridas llanuras rompen contra el Mare Magnum, la presencia de los espíritus del agua es pura y omnipresente. En lugar de habitar en salas atronadoras o ciudades ajetreadas, Islen prefiere este tranquilo puesto de avanzada, dedicando sus días a escuchar las mareas y a ayudar a los chamanes que buscan la comunión con el fluido elemento.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Shaman"]="Islen is an essential mentor on your journey, guiding you through the elemental rites needed to bind and commune with the spirits of water to earn your Water Totem.",["faction:Horde"]="Stationed along the Barrens coast, Islen serves as a tranquil Horde spiritual anchor, welcoming travelers from Orgrimmar and Thunder Bluff alike.",["race:Tauren"]="Islen embodies the traditional tauren reverence for the Earth Mother's gifts, choosing a solitary life by the sea to stay attuned to the subtle currents of the wild."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Islen Waterseer is a wise tauren shaman who resides along the coast of the Barrens at the Tidus Stair. She possesses a rare, deep bond with the elemental spirits of water and acts as a spiritual mentor for shamans journeying to earn their Water Totem.",["al"]={"islen waterseer lore","who is islen","tidus stair tauren"},["q"]="Who is Islen Waterseer?"},{["a"]="Horde shamans are directed to Islen by their trainers in Durotar, Orgrimmar, and Thunder Bluff during the Call of Water trials. She tests their understanding of the element and instructs them on crafting the Water Sapta to perceive water elementals directly.",["al"]={"why visit islen","call of water npc","shaman quest barrens coast"},["q"]="Why do shamans travel to see her?"},{["a"]="She can be found sitting outside a small fishing hut on the Tidus Stair, situated on the eastern shoreline of the Barrens, south of the Merchant Coast.",["al"]={"islen location","where is islen waterseer","find islen"},["q"]="Where is Islen Waterseer located?"},{["a"]="The Water Sapta is a specially brewed spiritual draught crafted through elemental components. Consuming it allows a shaman's sight to penetrate the physical plane and witness the hidden spirits of water dwelling in sacred springs and tides.",["al"]={"water sapta meaning","what does the sapta do"},["q"]="What is the Water Sapta she speaks of?"},{["a"]="Greta Mosshoof is an old tauren companion and fellow practitioner of spiritual crafts. The two share an enduring friendship, consulting one another on spiritual cleansing and the restorative nature of water.",["al"]={"greta mosshoof connection","islen friend"},["q"]="Who is Islen's friend Greta Mosshoof?"},{["a"]="Islen is allied with the Horde and the United Tauren Tribes under Cairne Bloodhoof. Though she lives in isolation along the coast, she readily aids orc, troll, and tauren shamans sent by the Horde's elders.",["al"]={"islen faction","is islen horde"},["q"]="Does Islen belong to a specific faction or tribe?"}},["kw"]={"barrens","call of water","greta mosshoof","islen","shaman","tidus stair","water sapta","waterseer"},["n"]="Islen Waterseer",["s"]="Islen Waterseer is a respected tauren shaman who dwells beside a quiet fishing hut on the Tidus Stair, overlooking the eastern sea of the Barrens. Possessing an intimate communion with the spirits of water, she guides initiates on the trials necessary to attune with the element. Novice shamans across the Horde seek her wisdom to earn their Water Totem.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Far from the bustling crossroads and encampments of the Barrens, Islen Waterseer lives along the craggy coastline known as the Tidus Stair. Here, where the arid plains break against the Great Sea, the presence of the water spirits is raw and pervasive. Rather than dwelling in thunderous halls or busy cities, Islen prefers this quiet outpost, dedicating her days to listening to the tides and assisting shamans who seek communion with the fluid element.",["t"]="The Hermit of Tidus Stair"},{["b"]="Understanding water requires more than simple study; it demands internal harmony and spiritual perception. Islen guides seekers through the preparation of the Water Sapta, a sacred brew that pierces the veil between mortal senses and elemental manifestations. Her teachings remind shamans that water is as unyielding and deep as it is fluid and restorative, requiring immense respect from any who hope to call upon its aid.",["t"]="Mistress of the Water Sapta"},{["b"]="While Islen maintains a quiet life on the coast, her spiritual reach and connections extend across Kalimdor. She maintains a close, enduring friendship with Greta Mosshoof, another wise tauren versed in the restorative arts. Through these connections, Islen's knowledge of water's purifying essence touches matters well beyond the Barrens, even offering spiritual aid to lands afflicted by deep corruption.",["t"]="Bonds Across the Wilds"}}}}}
t["npc:iverron"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="7,253,13.356.0,18.356.1,15.205.0,22.159.0,21.195.0,27.130.0,23.158.0,45.160.0",["h"]="290334",["n"]="Iverron",["s"]="Iverron. Iverron es un joven elfo de la noche que se encuentra en Cañada Umbría, la resguardada rama inicial de Teldrassil. Afectado por el veneno de los arácnidos cada vez más alterados del bosque, su desdicha sirve como una advertencia temprana de la creciente corrupción en el Árbol del Mundo. Mientras deambulaba por el tranquilo dosel de Cañada Umbría, Iverron tropezó con las arañas tejemadera que anidan en el valle. Sucumbiendo rápidamente a su mordedura tóxica, el joven elfo quedó incapacitado, incapaz de regresar a un lugar seguro por sus propios medios. Su estado de indefensión pone de manifiesto la repentina agresividad que invade a criaturas que antes compartían el claro en paz.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Druids studying in Shadowglen view Iverron's poisoning as a symptom of a deeper affliction gripping nature, requiring remedies forged directly from the flora and fauna of the glade.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Iverron's survival depends on the prompt gathering of local Shadowglen flora, emphasizing the critical value of herbal knowledge in preserving life.",["race:NightElf"]="For fledgling night elves taking their first steps outside Aldrassil, Iverron's misfortune is an early lesson in how quickly the wilds of Teldrassil are falling into imbalance."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Iverron is a young night elf dwelling in Shadowglen within Teldrassil. During his travels through the woodland, he fell victim to the poisonous fauna haunting the boughs and required urgent aid to survive.",["al"]={"iverron lore","who is iverron","iverron night elf"},["q"]="Who is Iverron?"},{["a"]="He was bitten by the aggressive webwood spiders that inhabit the thickets of Shadowglen, suffering from a debilitating venom that standard rest could not cure.",["al"]={"why is iverron sick","what bit iverron","iverron poison"},["q"]="What poisoned Iverron?"},{["a"]="He is cured through a concoction made of local Teldrassil plant matter, including hyacinth mushrooms and moonpetal lilies, mixed with webwood ichor from the spiders to create a targeted antidote.",["al"]={"cure iverron","iverron antidote","saving iverron"},["q"]="How is Iverron cured?"},{["a"]="He is located in Shadowglen, the secluded starting glade in the crown of Teldrassil where novice night elves begin their training.",["al"]={"iverron location","where is iverron","find iverron"},["q"]="Where can Iverron be found?"},{["a"]="Iverron sends adventurers to his friend Dirania Silvershine, who gathers the ingredients for an antidote and sends it back to him before it loses its potency.",["al"]={"who saves iverron","iverron friends","dentaria silverglade iverron"},["q"]="Who is helping Iverron?"},{["a"]="The sudden aggression of Shadowglen's spiders is part of an unnatural malady creeping into Teldrassil, warping normally reclusive beasts into violent predators.",["al"]={"why spiders attack","teldrassil spider corruption"},["q"]="Why are the spiders in Shadowglen so hostile?"}},["kw"]={"antidote","dentaria","iverron","kaldorei","shadowglen","spider","teldrassil","venom"},["n"]="Iverron",["s"]="Iverron is a young night elf found in Shadowglen, the sheltered starting bough of Teldrassil. Stricken by the venom of the woodland's increasingly agitated arachnids, his plight serves as an early warning of the growing corruption within the World Tree.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While wandering through the quiet canopies of Shadowglen, Iverron ran afoul of the webwood spiders nesting in the vale. Succumbing quickly to their toxic bite, the young elf was left incapacitated, unable to return to safety on his own. His helpless condition highlights the sudden aggression sweeping through creatures that once shared the glade in peace.",["t"]="A Bitter Bite"},{["b"]="Iverron's survival falls upon the quick thinking of his companions and local healers, who require potent woodland ingredients—such as hyacinth mushrooms, moonpetal lilies and webwood ichor—to brew an antidote. His brush with death is a sober reminder to all young kaldorei in Shadowglen that the boughs of Teldrassil are far from unblemished sanctuary.",["t"]="Desperate Remedies"}}}}}
t["npc:jaina-proudmoore"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,283,18.679.0,21.631.0,29.218.0,57.265.0,44.259.0,55.332.0",["h"]="57573a",["n"]="Jaina Valiente",["s"]="Jaina Valiente. Lady Jaina Valiente es la gobernante de Isla Theramore y la hechicera humana más poderosa con vida. Antigua alumna estrella del Kirin Tor de Dalaran, guio a los supervivientes de Lordaeron a través del Mare Magnum y ahora se esfuerza por mantener una frágil paz entre la Alianza y la nueva Horda. Hija del gran almirante Daelin Valiente de Kul Tiras, Jaina mostró una notable aptitud para lo arcano a temprana edad y estudió con el archimago Antonidas en Dalaran. Durante la Tercera Guerra, investigó la misteriosa Plaga de la no-muerte junto al príncipe Arthas Menethil, presenciando de primera mano la trágica caída de Lordaeron. Guiada por las advertencias del profeta Medivh, reunió una expedición de supervivientes humanos y zarpó hacia el oeste, rumbo al olvidado continente de Kalimdor. Allí, sus fuerzas forjaron una alianza sin precedentes con la Horda de Thrall y los elfos de la noche, manteniéndose unidos en la cima del Monte Hyjal para derrotar a Archimonde y hacer añicos la invasión de la Legión Ardiente.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="Trained under Archmage Antonidas himself, Lady Jaina is widely considered the most powerful living human sorceress, demonstrating the height of Dalaran's arcane mastery.",["faction:Alliance"]="Jaina provides the Alliance with its critical foothold in southern Kalimdor, balancing loyalty to Highlord Bolvar's regency in Stormwind against her desire to avoid war with the neighboring Horde."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Jaina is the ruler of Theramore Isle and arguably the most gifted human mage alive. She is the daughter of the late Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore of Kul Tiras and a former apprentice of Archmage Antonidas in Dalaran.",["al"]={"who is jaina","jaina proudmoore lore","theramore leader"},["q"]="Who is Lady Jaina Proudmoore?"},{["a"]="Before the fall of Lordaeron in the Third War, the Prophet Medivh warned Jaina to lead as many people as possible across the sea to Kalimdor. Her expedition survived the journey, fought at Mount Hyjal, and settled the port-fortress of Theramore in Dustwallow Marsh.",["al"]={"why did jaina leave lordaeron","jaina kalimdor","why is theramore here"},["q"]="Why is Jaina in Kalimdor instead of the Eastern Kingdoms?"},{["a"]="Jaina maintains an unusual, cautious friendship with Warchief Thrall. After fighting together against the Burning Legion at Mount Hyjal, both leaders have strived to keep the peace between their peoples, despite sharp opposition from hardliners on both sides.",["al"]={"is jaina friendly with thrall","jaina and horde","does jaina hate orcs"},["q"]="What is Jaina's relationship with the Horde?"},{["a"]="Jaina and Arthas were childhood friends whose bond deepened into romance as young adults. They jointly investigated the plague spreading across Lordaeron, but Jaina was horrified by Arthas's descent into ruthlessness—culminating in the purging of Stratholme, where she refused to participate in the slaughter of infected citizens.",["al"]={"jaina and arthas","did jaina love arthas"},["q"]="What happened between Jaina and Prince Arthas Menethil?"}},["kw"]={"antonidas","arthas","dustwallow","jaina","kirin tor","proudmoore","theramore","thrall"},["n"]="Jaina Proudmoore",["s"]="Lady Jaina Proudmoore is the ruler of Theramore Isle and the most powerful human sorceress alive. Formerly a star pupil of Dalaran's Kirin Tor, she led the survivors of Lordaeron across the Great Sea and now strives to maintain a fragile peace between the Alliance and the New Horde.",["sec"]={{["b"]="The daughter of Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore of Kul Tiras, Jaina showed remarkable aptitude for the arcane at an early age and studied under Archmage Antonidas in Dalaran. During the Third War, she investigated the mysterious Plague of Undeath alongside Prince Arthas Menethil, witnessing firsthand the tragic downfall of Lordaeron. Guided by the warnings of the Prophet Medivh, she rallied an expedition of human survivors and set sail westward to the forgotten continent of Kalimdor. There, her forces forged an unprecedented alliance with Thrall's Horde and the night elves, standing together atop Mount Hyjal to defeat Archimonde and shatter the Burning Legion's invasion.",["t"]="Flight to Kalimdor"},{["b"]="Following the Legion's defeat, Jaina founded the island citadel of Theramore off the coast of Dustwallow Marsh, establishing the primary bastion of the Alliance in southern Kalimdor. Her commitment to diplomacy was tested to its limits when her father arrived seeking vengeance against the orcs; Jaina refused to support his war, stepping aside as Thrall's forces slew the Grand Admiral to prevent Kalimdor from plunging into another devastating conflict. Today, she rules Theramore as a steadfast advocate for coexistence, working closely with Warchief Thrall while anchoring the Alliance's presence against rising local tensions.",["t"]="The Lady of Theramore"}}}}}
t["npc:je-neu-sancrea"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,300,22.452.0,19.449.1,22.215.0,71.296.0,50.299.0,32.174.0,25.212.0,57.225.0",["h"]="526157",["n"]="Je'neu Sancrea",["s"]="Je'neu Sancrea. Je'neu Sancrea es un trol de Lanza Negra y miembro del Anillo de la Tierra apostado en la Avanzada de Zoram'gar, a lo largo de la costa de Vallefresno. Al percibir oscuras perturbaciones en las profundidades de la costa, dirige a los aventureros de la Horda para investigar la corrupción que infesta el antiguo templo sumergido de las Cavernas de Brazanegra. Mientras la mayor parte del Anillo de la Tierra se centra en la armonía elemental por todo Kalimdor, Je'neu Sancrea vigila la aislada y peligrosa La Ensanada de Zoram. Establecido en la Avanzada de Zoram'gar, observa los oscuros temblores y las mareas antinaturales que se agitan cerca del templo en ruinas de las Cavernas de Brazanegra. Aunque está sujeto a los deberes chamánicos de su círculo, su fuerte lealtad a la tribu Lanza Negra y a la Horda de Thrall hace que trabaje exclusivamente junto a los campeones de la Horda.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Shaman"]="As a prominent Darkspear member of the Earthen Ring, Je'neu represents the shamanic duty to balance corrupted elementals and restore balance to the waters of Kalimdor.",["faction:Horde"]="Je'neu serves as the Horde's primary quest hub and lore guide for entering the depths of Blackfathom Deeps from Ashenvale.",["race:Troll"]="Je'neu demonstrates how Darkspear trolls have embraced the spiritual paths of the Earthen Ring alongside their tauren and orc allies."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Je'neu Sancrea is a Darkspear troll shaman affiliated with the Earthen Ring. He is stationed at Zoram'gar Outpost on the Ashenvale coast, where he monitors the growing corruption spilling out from Blackfathom Deeps.",["al"]={"who is jeneu","jeneu sancrea lore","what is jeneu"},["q"]="Who is Je'neu Sancrea?"},{["a"]="Although the Earthen Ring as an organization pursues elemental balance rather than faction warfare, Je'neu's personal ties remain firmly rooted in the Darkspear tribe and the Horde. Because he resides within a frontline Horde military outpost in Ashenvale, he does not welcome Alliance travelers.",["al"]={"why horde only","can alliance talk to jeneu","is jeneu neutral"},["q"]="Why does Je'neu only deal with Horde adventurers if he is Earthen Ring?"},{["a"]="Je'neu investigates the unnatural elemental unrest and dark magic rising from Blackfathom Deeps. He charges champions with retrieving corrupted water cores, slaying Twilight's Hammer cultists, and confirming whispers that an ancient hydra, Aku'mai, serves ancient malevolent masters beneath the sea.",["al"]={"jeneu quest goals","what does jeneu want","why send players to bfd"},["q"]="What is Je'neu investigating in Blackfathom Deeps?"},{["a"]="Je'neu is located at Zoram'gar Outpost, a fortified Horde settlement on the far northwestern coast of Ashenvale, right along the Zoram Strand just south of Blackfathom Deeps.",["al"]={"where is jeneu","jeneu sancrea location","find jeneu"},["q"]="Where is Je'neu Sancrea located?"},{["a"]="The Earthen Ring is an ancient circle of shamans dedicated to understanding and soothing the elemental spirits of the world, intervening whenever dark forces or chaotic entities disrupt natural elemental harmony.",["al"]={"earthen ring lore","what is the earthen ring","shaman organization"},["q"]="What is the Earthen Ring?"},{["a"]="The Twilight's Hammer cult has infiltrated Blackfathom Deeps to venerate the beast Aku'mai and conduct rituals dedicated to the Old Gods. Je'neu tasks Horde adventurers with cutting down their leaders to halt their dark work.",["al"]={"twilights hammer bfd","twilight cult ashenvale","who are the cultists in bfd"},["q"]="What is the threat of the Twilight's Hammer in the Deeps?"}},["kw"]={"aku'mai","blackfathom deeps","earthen ring","je'neu sancrea","jeneu","twilight's hammer","zoram strand","zoram'gar outpost"},["n"]="Je'neu Sancrea",["s"]="Je'neu Sancrea is a Darkspear troll and a member of the Earthen Ring stationed at Zoram'gar Outpost along the Ashenvale coast. Sensing dark disturbances deep beneath the shoreline, he directs Horde adventurers to investigate the corruption infesting the ancient submerged temple of Blackfathom Deeps.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While most of the Earthen Ring focuses on elemental harmony across Kalimdor, Je'neu Sancrea keeps watch over the secluded and dangerous Zoram Strand. Perched at Zoram'gar Outpost, he observes the dark tremors and unnatural tides stirring near the ruined temple of Blackfathom Deeps. Though bound by the shamanic duties of his circle, his strong loyalties to the Darkspear tribe and Thrall's Horde keep him working exclusively alongside Horde champions.",["t"]="A Shaman on the Strand"},{["b"]="Je'neu seeks to uncover the true cause behind the creeping corruption around the coast. Through bold adventurers, he collects tainted sapphire cores, investigates the vile remnants of water elementals like Baron Aquanis, and uncovers the insidious influence of the Twilight's Hammer cult. The dark rituals taking place beneath the waves threaten not only the balance of the local elements, but herald the dark return of forces sworn to the Old Gods.",["t"]="Shadows of the Deep"}}}}}
t["npc:jern-hornhelm"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,350,22.390.0,29.391.0,21.187.0,31.113.0,42.148.0,58.279.0,48.234.0,53.223.0",["h"]="8dadcb",["n"]="Jern Cornamenta",["s"]="Jern Cornamenta. Jern Cornamenta es un minero enano afiliado a la Liga de Expedicionarios, apostado en el poblado de Thelsamar. Coordina la logística vital y la comunicación entre el asentamiento, Forjaz y el yacimiento arqueológico situado más al interior de Loch Modan. Los aventureros le ayudan con frecuencia transportando suministros de minería e informes de progresos por toda la región. Apostado en el rústico poblado de Thelsamar, Jern Cornamenta desempeña un papel logístico clave para las operaciones de los enanos en todo Loch Modan. Mientras los eruditos y los equipos de campo enanos se adentran en las tierras salvajes para desenterrar su pasado ancestral, mantener unas cadenas de suministro constantes sigue siendo esencial. Jern se asegura de que los recursos vitales, las herramientas y las comunicaciones lleguen sanos y salvos a las excavaciones activas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance travelers passing through Loch Modan find Jern to be an essential point of contact for securing the region and maintaining dwarven infrastructure.",["profession:Mining"]="Miners will appreciate Jern's trade background and practical understanding of subterranean logistics, blasting, and resource hauling.",["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, assisting Jern directly advances the sacred quest to uncover the race's ancient Titan heritage buried deep within the mountains."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Jern Hornhelm is a dwarven miner and logistics coordinator based in Thelsamar in Loch Modan. He works on behalf of the Explorers' League to keep local excavation efforts running smoothly.",["al"]={"who is jern","jern hornhelm identity","thelsamar dwarf jern"},["q"]="Who is Jern Hornhelm?"},{["a"]="He can be found standing outdoors in the town of Thelsamar, situated centrally in Loch Modan along the main road.",["al"]={"jern hornhelm location","where is jern","jern hornhelm map"},["q"]="Where can I find Jern Hornhelm?"},{["a"]="Jern is aligned with the Alliance and specifically represents the dwarven Explorers' League, managing the movement of personnel and mining supplies.",["al"]={"jern hornhelm faction","who does jern work for","is jern explorers league"},["q"]="What faction does Jern Hornhelm belong to?"},{["a"]="Archaeological digs in the mountainous terrain require controlled demolitions to break through stubborn rock faces. Jern coordinates the delivery of specialized blasting powder to Prospector Ironband's dig site so the crew can safely uncover Titan relics and ancient stone halls.",["al"]={"powder to ironband lore","why excavation needs powder","blasting powder loch modan"},["q"]="Why does Jern need blasting powder sent to the excavation?"},{["a"]="Jern serves as a vital communications link between remote digs in Loch Modan and the high leadership of the Explorers' League located in Ironforge's Hall of Explorers, frequently dispatching field progress reports back to the capital.",["al"]={"jern hornhelm ironforge","report to ironforge jern"},["q"]="What is Jern Hornhelm's connection to Ironforge?"},{["a"]="The sudden rise of aggressive troggs displaced from beneath the earth has severely threatened excavation efforts and blocked trade routes, making regular delivery runs dangerous without armed adventurers to escort supplies.",["al"]={"ironband excavation problems","loch modan dig dangers","why jern needs help"},["q"]="What problems are the dig sites facing in Loch Modan?"}},["kw"]={"blasting powder","excavation","explorers' league","ironband","jern hornhelm","loch modan","miner","thelsamar"},["n"]="Jern Hornhelm",["s"]="Jern Hornhelm is a dwarven miner affiliated with the Explorers' League, stationed in the town of Thelsamar. He coordinates vital logistics and communication between the settlement, Ironforge, and the archaeological dig site deeper in Loch Modan. Adventurers frequently assist him with shuttling mining supplies and progress reports across the region.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Stationed within the rustic town of Thelsamar, Jern Hornhelm plays a key logistical role for dwarven operations throughout Loch Modan. While dwarven scholars and field teams venture out into the wilderness to unearth their ancestral past, maintaining consistent supply chains remains essential. Jern ensures that vital resources, tools, and communications reach the active dig sites safely.",["t"]="Logistics in Thelsamar"},{["b"]="As a member of the Explorers' League, Jern bridges the gap between field archaeologists and the League's leadership in the Hall of Explorers in Ironforge. Sites such as Ironband's Excavation rely heavily on blasting powder, equipment, and regular dispatches to keep work moving forward. Jern enlists reliable travelers to navigate the trogg-infested roads and keep the dig fully operational.",["t"]="Serving the Explorers' League"}}}}}
t["npc:jonathan-carevin"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,277,19.410.0,24.412.1,24.160.0,40.231.0,27.137.0,48.203.0,36.171.0,37.170.0",["h"]="cbe5a9",["n"]="Jonathan Carevin",["s"]="Jonathan Carevin. Jonathan Carevin es un decidido cazador humano que reside en Villa Oscura, entregado a erradicar la oscuridad que asola Bosque del Ocaso. A diferencia de la defensiva Guardia Nocturna, él y su familia cazan activamente a los no-muertos, huargen y cualquier amenaza herética que aceche bajo las sombrías copas de los árboles. Aunque Villa Oscura depende de la Guardia Nocturna para patrullar los caminos y proteger el pueblo, Jonathan Carevin cree que un mero perímetro defensivo no basta. Junto a su familia y aliados como Calor, Jonathan toma la ofensiva. Pone en su punto de mira a los engendros profanos que deambulan por Bosque del Ocaso, embarcándose en una cruzada personal para purgar a todos los demonios, no-muertos y herejes de la región bajo la gracia de la Luz.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Hunter"]="Hunters find common ground with Carevin's proactive tracking and methodical culling of Duskwood's nocturnal predators.",["class:Paladin"]="Carevin's zeal and invocation of the Light against demonic and undead corruption resonate deeply with a paladin's sacred vows.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance champions trying to stabilize Duskwood, Jonathan Carevin provides targeted strikes against the supernatural threats that Stormwind's neglect has left unchecked."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Jonathan Carevin is a grim hunter living in Darkshire in Duskwood. He leads the Carevin family in an active fight against the foul monsters haunting the forest.",["al"]={"who is carevin","jonathan carevin lore","carevin darkshire"},["q"]="Who is Jonathan Carevin?"},{["a"]="While the Night Watch focuses primarily on guarding Darkshire's perimeter and keeping the roads passable, Jonathan and his supporters actively track and hunt down the undead and other abominations to eradicate them at their source.",["al"]={"is he night watch","carevin vs night watch"},["q"]="How does he differ from the Night Watch?"},{["a"]="Jonathan actively hunts the undead, ravenous worgen packs, demons, and anyone who would offer shelter or aid to such unholy abominations.",["al"]={"what does carevin hunt","carevin targets"},["q"]="What threats does he fight?"},{["a"]="His harsh rhetoric, fervent devotion to the Light, and strict zero-tolerance approach toward corruption mirror Scarlet beliefs, but officially he operates independently alongside his family in Darkshire.",["al"]={"carevin scarlet crusade","is carevin scarlet"},["q"]="Is Jonathan affiliated with the Scarlet Crusade?"},{["a"]="Beyond his immediate family, Jonathan receives direct assistance from sympathetic combatants such as Calor, who aids him in tracking monstrous incursions across the woods.",["al"]={"carevin allies","who helps carevin"},["q"]="Who assists Jonathan in his mission?"},{["a"]="Jonathan views the worgen as an unnatural menace terrorizing Duskwood's people and tasks travelers with uncovering the source of their sudden emergence in the wilderness.",["al"]={"carevin worgen","why carevin hate worgen"},["q"]="What is his connection to the worgen?"}},["kw"]={"calor","carevin family","darkshire","duskwood","jonathan carevin","night watch","undead","worgen"},["n"]="Jonathan Carevin",["s"]="Jonathan Carevin is a resolute human hunter residing in Darkshire, dedicated to eradicating the darkness plaguing Duskwood. Unlike the defensive Night Watch, he and his family actively hunt down the undead, worgen, and any heretical threats lurking under the darkened canopies.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While Darkshire depends upon the Night Watch to patrol the roads and safeguard the township, Jonathan Carevin believes a mere defensive perimeter is insufficient. Alongside his family and allies like Calor, Jonathan takes the offensive. He actively targets the unholy fiends wandering Duskwood, pursuing a personal crusade to purge all demons, undead, and heretics from the region under the grace of the Light.",["t"]="The Carevin Crusade"},{["b"]="Jonathan's vigilance extends beyond shambling skeletons and ghouls. He pays close attention to the savage, wolf-like beasts known as worgen that stalk the forest depths. Knowing the danger they present to an already besieged settlement, Jonathan coordinates investigations into their mysterious presence, seeking to uncover where these ungodly predators originated and putting an end to their nocturnal prowling.",["t"]="The Shadow of the Worgen"}}}}}
t["npc:jordan-stilwell"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,358,22.527.0,22.418.0,22.491.1,23.230.0,78.181.0,56.266.0,23.160.0,45.178.0,30.192.0",["h"]="bcac66",["n"]="Jordan Fontana",["s"]="Jordan Fontana. Jordan Fontana es un diestro forjador de armas humano apostado a las afueras de las nevadas Puertas de Forjaz, en Dun Morogh. Aunque en un principio estaba destinado a convertirse en paladín de la Luz Sagrada, siguió el oficio de su padre para convertirse en un artesano cuyo trabajo sirve a los paladines de toda la Alianza. Es conocido sobre todo por forjar el Puño de Verigan en honor a su viejo amigo, Bosch Verigan. Aunque se esperaba que Jordan Fontana tomara los votos sagrados y se convirtiera en paladín de la Iglesia de la Luz Sagrada, al final eligió el camino de la forja. Siguió los pasos de su padre empuñando el martillo de herrero encantado de este. Jordan perfeccionó su oficio bajo la tutela del herrero enano Bailor Petramano. A pesar de dejar a un lado el manto de guerrero sagrado ungido, Jordan sigue siendo profundamente fiel a la Luz, dedicando su extraordinaria maestría a equipar a los campeones que luchan en su nombre.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Paladin"]="Jordan Stilwell is a crucial figure in a paladin's early trials, tasking them with scouring Azeroth for rare components to forge their signature warhammer, Verigan's Fist.",["faction:Alliance"]="Having fled the horrors of Arugal's worgen in Silverpine Forest, Jordan found sanctuary with the dwarves of Dun Morogh and now lends his craft directly to Alliance champions.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Trained by the dwarf Bailor Stonehand and wielding an enchanted hammer inherited from his father, Jordan represents the pinnacle of mortal holy metalworking."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Jordan Stilwell is a master human blacksmith found working outside the Gates of Ironforge in Dun Morogh. He crafts sacred armaments for paladins of the Church of the Holy Light, most notably the legendary warhammer Verigan's Fist.",["al"]={"who is jordan stilwell","jordan stilwell lore","who is this blacksmith outside ironforge"},["q"]="Who is Jordan Stilwell?"},{["a"]="According to Duthorian Rall in Stormwind, Jordan prefers working in the crisp, cool mountain air of Dun Morogh rather than the stifling interior of the Great Forge within Ironforge.",["al"]={"why is jordan outside ironforge","why work in dun morogh","why is he in the snow"},["q"]="Why does Jordan Stilwell work outside in the snow instead of inside Ironforge?"},{["a"]="Jordan was once an armorer and blacksmith stationed at Baron Silverlaine's estate in Silverpine Forest. He managed to flee the keep before or during the disastrous uprising when Archmage Arugal and his feral worgen slaughtered the garrison and overtook the fortress.",["al"]={"jordan stilwell shadowfang keep","jordan stilwell silverpine","did he live in pyrewood"},["q"]="What is Jordan Stilwell's connection to Shadowfang Keep?"},{["a"]="Verigan's Fist is a powerful two-handed holy hammer forged by Jordan Stilwell for Alliance paladins. It is named in honor of Jordan's old friend, Bosch Verigan.",["al"]={"verigans fist","verigan hammer","who is verigan"},["q"]="What is Verigan's Fist?"},{["a"]="Jordan inherited his craft and an enchanted smithing hammer from his father, and went on to refine his expertise under the instruction of the dwarven blacksmith Bailor Stonehand.",["al"]={"who trained jordan stilwell","jordan stilwell teacher","where did he learn smithing"},["q"]="Who trained Jordan Stilwell in blacksmithing?"},{["a"]="Jordan is married to Daphne Stilwell. Together, the couple has provided immense aid to the Church of the Holy Light over the years, and both are revered as deeply devout servants of the faith.",["al"]={"jordan stilwell wife","daphne stilwell husband","daphne stilwell"},["q"]="Who is Jordan Stilwell's wife?"}},["kw"]={"bailor stonehand","bosch verigan","daphne stilwell","dun morogh","ironforge","jordan stilwell","shadowfang keep","tome of valor","verigan's fist","verigans fist"},["n"]="Jordan Stilwell",["s"]="Jordan Stilwell is a skilled human weaponsmith stationed outside the snowy Gates of Ironforge in Dun Morogh. Though originally meant to become a paladin of the Holy Light, he followed his father's craft to become an artisan whose work serves paladins across the Alliance. He is best known for forging Verigan's Fist in honor of his old friend, Bosch Verigan.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Though Jordan Stilwell was expected to take holy vows and become a paladin within the Church of the Holy Light, he ultimately chose the way of the forge. He followed in his father's footsteps, taking up his father's enchanted smithing hammer. Jordan refined his craft under the tutelage of the dwarven blacksmith Bailor Stonehand. Despite setting aside the mantle of an anointed holy warrior, Jordan remains deeply faithful to the Light, dedicating his extraordinary craftsmanship to outfitting champions who fight in its name.",["t"]="A Calling at the Anvil"},{["b"]="Long before setting up shop in the biting cold of Dun Morogh, Jordan served as a smith at the keep of Baron Silverlaine in Silverpine Forest. When Archmage Arugal unleashed the feral worgen upon the fortress, turning it into the cursed bastion known as Shadowfang Keep, Jordan managed to escape the bloodshed. Forced to abandon his forge and his former home, he eventually found refuge among the dwarves of Dun Morogh.",["t"]="Flight from Silverpine"},{["b"]="Jordan keeps his forge outdoors near the gates of Ironforge, favoring the brisk alpine air over the stifling heat of the Great Forge inside the mountain. When the Church of the Holy Light sends worthy paladins to him, Jordan tasks them with recovering rare materials from across the world to craft a legendary two-handed warhammer. Named Verigan's Fist in honor of his old friend Bosch Verigan, the weapon stands as a testament to the enduring bond between devoted faith and masterful steel.",["t"]="Forging Verigan's Fist"}}}}}
t["npc:kadrak"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="6,379,23.446.0,19.406.0,14.173.0,26.155.0,35.187.0,45.165.0,44.190.0,53.167.0",["h"]="c70364",["n"]="Kadrak",["s"]="Kadrak. Kadrak es un curtido comandante orco apostado en La Muralla de Mor'shan, en la frontera entre Los Baldíos y Vallefresno. Con la tarea de salvaguardar la frontera norte, coordina la llegada de despachos y refuerzos al disputado bosque. Para los aventureros de la Horda que avanzan más allá de las llanuras áridas, Kadrak actúa como la puerta de entrada a la incesante lucha contra los elfos de la noche. Apostado en lo alto de las barricadas fortificadas de madera de La Muralla de Mor'shan, Kadrak vigila la ruta principal que conecta Los Baldíos con Vallefresno. La frontera es un límite precario: al sur se extienden las llanuras abrasadas por el sol reclamadas por la Horda, mientras que al norte se alzan los antiguos bosques defendidos con fiereza por los elfos de la noche. Kadrak se asegura de que el perímetro defensivo permanezca intacto frente a las incursiones de las Centinelas y las hostiles criaturas del bosque.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warrior"]="Kadrak embodies frontline discipline, relying on raw steel and martial strength to hold a fortified choke point against hostile woodcraft and guerrilla raids.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance forces attempting to strike into the Barrens from Ashenvale, Kadrak and his rampart represent a fortified roadblock guarding the Horde's heartland.",["faction:Horde"]="Kadrak is your entry point to Ashenvale's campaigns, directing the flow of warriors northward to defend lumber operations and carve out Horde territory.",["race:Orc"]="As a steadfast veteran upholding the legacy of the Warsong Clan's territorial efforts, Kadrak represents the unyielding orcish resolve on the Ashenvale border."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Kadrak is an orc officer stationed at the Mor'shan Rampart. He oversees border security and directs Horde forces traveling between the Barrens and the warzones of Ashenvale.",["al"]={"kadrak identity","who is the orc at the wall","mor'shan rampart commander"},["q"]="Who is Kadrak?"},{["a"]="Kadrak stands at the Mor'shan Rampart, the fortified wooden barricade at the far northern edge of the Barrens, marking the boundary leading into Ashenvale.",["al"]={"kadrak location","find kadrak","where is kadrak"},["q"]="Where can Kadrak be found?"},{["a"]="He commands the defensive perimeter at the border, gathers military intelligence from scout runners, and briefs Horde travelers heading north to reinforce outposts like Splintertree Post.",["al"]={"kadrak duties","what does kadrak do","kadrak role"},["q"]="What is Kadrak's role in the Horde?"},{["a"]="The Rampart protects the northern approaches of the Barrens and Durotar from retaliatory night elf incursions sparked by the Horde's logging operations in Ashenvale.",["al"]={"why is mor'shan rampart fortified","purpose of the rampart","why guard ashenvale border"},["q"]="Why is the Mor'shan Rampart heavily defended?"},{["a"]="Kadrak receives reports carried from the Barrens and dispatches adventurers on missions regarding Warsong scouting reports and establishing a firmer Horde presence along the forest frontier.",["al"]={"kadrak quests","report to kadrak","the warsong reports"},["q"]="What quests does Kadrak provide or complete?"},{["a"]="Kadrak has ties to frontline Horde officers, including Captain Shatterskull, and maintains regular communication with the Warsong Outriders operating within Ashenvale.",["al"]={"kadrak connections","kadrak and shatterskull"},["q"]="Does Kadrak have ties to other notable Horde figures?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","barrens","kadrak","mor'shan rampart","orc","rampart","splintertree post","warsong"},["n"]="Kadrak",["s"]="Kadrak is a seasoned orc commander stationed at the Mor'shan Rampart on the border between the Barrens and Ashenvale. Tasked with safeguarding the northern frontier, he coordinates the flow of dispatches and reinforcements into the contested forest. For Horde adventurers pushing past the arid plains, Kadrak serves as the gateway to the ongoing struggle against the night elves.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Standing atop the fortified timber barricades of the Mor'shan Rampart, Kadrak watches over the primary route connecting the Barrens to Ashenvale. The border is a precarious frontier: to the south lie the sun-scorched plainsclaimed by the Horde, while to the north loom the ancient woods guarded fiercely by the night elves. Kadrak ensures that the defensive perimeter remains unbroken against encroaching Sentinels and hostile woodland creatures.",["t"]="Guardian of the Rampart"},{["b"]="Beyond holding the line, Kadrak manages essential military intelligence between the Barrens and the forward logging camps deeper in the forest. He receives couriers bearing critical combat reports from the Warsong Outriders and coordinates the movement of supplies and fresh blood into outpost hubs like Splintertree Post. Those reporting to him are promptly directed into the heart of the territorial war.",["t"]="Frontline Logistics"}}}}}
t["npc:kaela-shadowspear"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,351,23.446.0,16.414.0,25.216.0,37.179.0,25.158.0,44.178.0,54.185.0,36.230.0",["h"]="367721",["n"]="Kaela Lanzasombra",["s"]="Kaela Lanzasombra. Kaela Lanzasombra es una centinela elfa de la noche apostada al suroeste de Risco Cortaviento, en Sierra Espolón. Desde su pequeño puesto avanzado, se coordina con otras centinelas para vigilar la creciente tensión y las perturbaciones territoriales en la naturaleza. Confía en viajeros valientes para explorar el peligroso territorio y llevar ayuda a los defensores heridos de la tierra. Apostada justo al suroeste de la devastación industrial de Risco Cortaviento, Kaela Lanzasombra mantiene una atenta vigilancia sobre los pasos circundantes. Sierra Espolón está plagada de peligros a medida que la Horda avanza y las operaciones de los goblins explotan los recursos naturales de la zona. Operando junto al gnomo Gaxim Silvóxido, Kaela actúa como un enlace avanzado fundamental para los elfos de la noche, rastreando las amenazas que se adentran en territorio ancestral.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Druids will find common cause with Kaela's efforts to nurse injured ancients back to health and silence the agony of disturbed nature spirits.",["faction:Alliance"]="Kaela Shadowspear serves as a crucial point of contact for Alliance adventurers venturing into the contested reaches of Stonetalon, coordinating intelligence between distant outposts.",["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves, Kaela represents the steadfast defense of sacred ground, laboring to soothe outraged spirits and safeguard the revered ancients of Kalimdor."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Kaela Shadowspear is a night elf quest giver stationed in a frontier camp southwest of Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains. She oversees regional scouting and aids in protecting the local wildlife and spirits.",["al"]={"who is kaela","kaela shadowspear identity","kaela npc"},["q"]="Who is Kaela Shadowspear?"},{["a"]="She is located in a small Alliance camp situated southwest of Windshear Crag along the road in the Stonetalon Mountains, sharing the camp with the gnome engineer Gaxim Rustfizzle.",["al"]={"kaela shadowspear location","where is kaela","kaela stonetalon camp"},["q"]="Where can Kaela Shadowspear be found?"},{["a"]="Kaela coordinates closely with Sentinel Thenysil, regularly sending and receiving intelligence updates on enemy movements and local threats across Stonetalon.",["al"]={"kaela reports to who","kaela thenysil","kaela's commander"},["q"]="Who does Kaela report to?"},{["a"]="Intense logging, mining, and military encroachment in Stonetalon have deeply disturbed the natural balance, causing elemental spirits to fly into a rage and attack anyone nearby.",["al"]={"enraged spirits quest","why are spirits angry","kaela elemental spirits"},["q"]="Why is Kaela concerned about the elementals?"},{["a"]="The regional conflicts and rapid deforestation have left ancient protectors wounded and suffering. Kaela seeks the aid of travelers to find and heal these fallen protectors of the wild.",["al"]={"wounded ancients quest","kaela ancients","stonetalon wounded ancients"},["q"]="What is happening to the ancients near Windshear Crag?"},{["a"]="Kaela shares her camp with Gaxim Rustfizzle, an Alliance gnome. While Kaela focuses on the spiritual and tactical balance of the wilderness, Gaxim is concerned with counteracting the hostile goblin machinery and operations nearby.",["al"]={"gaxim rustfizzle kaela","why is gaxim with kaela","gnome and night elf camp"},["q"]="Why is a gnome stationed with Kaela?"}},["kw"]={"ancients","kaela","rustfizzle","sentinel","shadowspear","spirits","stonetalon","thenysil","windshear"},["n"]="Kaela Shadowspear",["s"]="Kaela Shadowspear is a night elf sentinel stationed southwest of Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains. From her small outpost, she coordinates with fellow sentinels to monitor escalating tensions and regional disruptions in the wilderness. She relies on brave travelers to scout dangerous territory and bring aid to the land's wounded defenders.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Positioned just southwest of the industrial devastation of Windshear Crag, Kaela Shadowspear keeps a watchful vigil over the surrounding passes. The Stonetalon Mountains are fraught with danger as the Horde encroaches and goblin operations exploit the land's natural bounty. Operating alongside the gnome Gaxim Rustfizzle, Kaela acts as an essential forward liaison for the night elves, tracking threats that push deeper into ancestral territory.",["t"]="A Scout on the Frontier"},{["b"]="The unrest in Stonetalon goes far beyond territorial skirmishes. The violent disruption of nature has agitated the elementals and brought harm to ancient guardians of the forest. Kaela works tirelessly to dispatch adventurers against raging elemental spirits and to tend to the wounded ancients suffering in the crossfire of the region's conflicts, striving to restore peace before the land is irrevocably scarred.",["t"]="Healing the Land"}}}}}
t["npc:kam-deepfury"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="12,301,24.459.0,25.447.0,17.404.1,20.226.0,58.266.0,47.242.0,28.238.0,40.154.0,52.125.0",["h"]="cb048f",["n"]="Kam Furiahonda",["s"]="Kam Furiahonda. Kam Furiahonda es un infame saboteador Hierro Negro encarcelado en las profundidades de las Mazmorras de Ventormenta. A diferencia de la mayoría de los reclusos de la prisión, no rinde lealtad a la Hermandad Defias, pues fue capturado tras orquestar una devastadora explosión a lo largo del Puente Thandol, muy al norte. Aunque Las Mazmorras están repletas en su inmensa mayoría de albañiles descontentos y rebeldes Defias, Kam Furiahonda es un caso aparte. Siendo un enano Hierro Negro tan astuto como violento, Furiahonda fue capturado y llevado a Ventormenta tras liderar una operación que inutilizó infraestructura vital en el norte. Se encuentra encerrado en lo más profundo de las celdas de la prisión, aislado de sus congéneres bajo la Montaña Roca Negra, pero tan hostil hacia la Alianza como cualquier amotinado que comparte los pasillos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="While most eyes in Stormwind are focused on the Defias uprising, Deepfury is a reminder of the broader Dark Iron menace threatening the northern frontiers of the Alliance.",["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves of Ironforge, Kam Deepfury is a bitter enemy whose sabotage severed the Thandol Span and murdered the kin of Longbraid the Grim. Avenging that loss is a point of personal honor."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Kam Deepfury is an elite Dark Iron dwarf prisoner locked inside the Stormwind Stockade. He is known for orchestrating the sabotage of the Thandol Span in the north and has no ties to the Defias rebels imprisoned alongside him.",["al"]={"who is deepfury","kam deepfury lore","who is the dwarf in stockades"},["q"]="Who is Kam Deepfury?"},{["a"]="Deepfury was captured after coordinating an attack that blew up one of the bridges at the Thandol Span, killing dwarven defenders and cutting off a vital land crossing between the Wetlands and Arathi. He was sent to Stormwind's high-security prison to await justice.",["al"]={"why is he in stockade","what did kam deepfury do","why is he imprisoned"},["q"]="Why is a Dark Iron dwarf locked in the Stormwind Stockade?"},{["a"]="No. Although he is imprisoned alongside the Defias Brotherhood during their uprising inside the Stockade, Deepfury belongs to the hostile Dark Iron clan. He acts entirely on his own clan's aggressive agenda against the Alliance and Ironforge.",["al"]={"is he defias","kam deepfury defias","is deepfury working with vancleef"},["q"]="Is Kam Deepfury part of the Defias Brotherhood?"},{["a"]="Motley Garmason and the Ironforge dwarven forces stationed at Dun Modr want him dead. Longbraid the Grim lost a relative in Deepfury's bombing of the Thandol Span, prompting them to send word to adventurers in Stormwind to claim his head.",["al"]={"who gave the quest for deepfury","who wants deepfury killed"},["q"]="Who wants Kam Deepfury dead?"},{["a"]="Deepfury organized the sabotage at the Thandol Span, the colossal bridge complex connecting the Wetlands with the Arathi Highlands far north of Stormwind.",["al"]={"where was the bridge blown up","deepfury bridge bombing","thandol span attack"},["q"]="Where did Kam Deepfury commit his crime?"},{["a"]="Kam Deepfury is held within the cell blocks of the Stormwind Stockade, situated beneath the canal district of Stormwind City.",["al"]={"where is deepfury in stockade","kam deepfury location"},["q"]="Where can Kam Deepfury be found inside the Stockade?"}},["kw"]={"dark iron","deepfury","dun modr","garmason","kam deepfury","longbraid","stockade","stormwind","thandol span"},["n"]="Kam Deepfury",["s"]="Kam Deepfury is a notorious Dark Iron saboteur incarcerated within the depths of the Stormwind Stockade. Unlike the majority of the prison's inmates, he has no allegiance to the Defias Brotherhood, having been captured for orchestrating a devastating explosion along the Thandol Span far to the north.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While the Stockade is overwhelmingly filled with disgruntled Stonemasons and Defias rebels, Kam Deepfury stands apart. A Dark Iron dwarf of cunning and violence, Deepfury was captured and brought to Stormwind after masterminding an operation that crippled vital northern infrastructure. He is locked deep within the prison's cells, isolated from his kin beneath Blackrock Mountain but just as hostile to the Alliance as any rebel rioter sharing the corridors.",["t"]="A Saboteur Far from Home"},{["b"]="Alliance intelligence stationed at Dun Modr, near the northern border of the Wetlands, identified Deepfury as the chief architect behind the explosion that shattered the Thandol Span. The blast severed one of the massive stone bridges linking the Wetlands to the Arathi Highlands. Beyond crippling a critical trade and military route for Ironforge and the Alliance, the sabotage claimed the life of a kin of the dwarf commander Longbraid the Grim.",["t"]="The Thandol Span Sabotage"},{["b"]="The Dark Iron insurrectionist did not manage to escape retribution for long, though imprisonment in Stormwind offered him temporary protection from his victims' relatives. Back in the Wetlands, Motley Garmason and the grieving Longbraid the Grim have sought mercenaries willing to infiltrate the riot-torn prison and sever Deepfury's head, settling a bloody grudge sparked hundreds of miles to the north.",["t"]="A Score to Settle"}}}}}
t["npc:lady-anacondra"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,388,27.516.0,22.419.0,34.172.0,45.267.0,40.229.0,42.196.0,52.169.0,37.176.0",["h"]="310ffb",["n"]="Lady Anacondra",["s"]="Lady Anacondra. Lady Anacondra es una de las Señoras del Colmillo que lideran a los Druidas del Colmillo en las Cuevas de los Lamentos. Antaño una acólita elfa de la noche llamada Scarletleaf, fue la primera en ofrecerse voluntaria para la ambiciosa empresa de Naralex de sanar Los Baldíos. Cuando la comunión de su maestro con el Sueño Esmeralda se convirtió en una pesadilla, su mente se quebró, retorciendo su devoción en un impulso venenoso por ver Kalimdor invadido por serpientes. Antes de adoptar su título serpentino, Lady Anacondra era conocida como Scarletleaf. Cuando el druida anciano Naralex ideó acceder a los manantiales subterráneos de Los Baldíos a través del Sueño Esmeralda, ella dio un paso al frente como su primerísima voluntaria. Su ferviente lealtad, sin embargo, supuso su perdición. Mientras la mente de Naralex caía presa de oscuras visiones, la pesadilla se filtró desde el reino onírico y contaminó a sus discípulos, destrozando la cordura de Scarletleaf y transformando su devoción en una fría obsesión reptiliana.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Anacondra represents a cautionary tragedy for Cenarion druids: an earnest acolyte whose zeal to heal the land made her vulnerable to the nightmare that twisted her communion into madness.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde cannot allow Anacondra and the Fanglords to threaten the delicate lifelines of the Barrens, making her removal critical to securing Crossroads and the nearby oases.",["race:NightElf"]="Seeing a sister of Kaldorei lineage discard her heritage and form in pursuit of a twisted serpentine dream is a sobering reminder of the perils lurking within the Emerald Dream."},["faq"]={{["a"]="She was originally a young night elf acolyte named Scarletleaf. She was the very first disciple to volunteer to accompany the druid Naralex on his mission into the Barrens.",["al"]={"anacondra real name","who is scarletleaf","scarletleaf backstory"},["q"]="Who was Lady Anacondra originally?"},{["a"]="When Naralex attempted to connect to the Emerald Dream beneath the Barrens, his thoughts were overrun by a nightmare. That same nightmare infected the minds of his acolytes, corrupting Scarletleaf and driving her to cast aside her old life to serve the twisted dream.",["al"]={"why is anacondra evil","how did she become a druid of the fang","why did scarletleaf fall"},["q"]="Why did she turn against the Cenarion Circle?"},{["a"]="She serves as one of the four Fanglords leading the Druids of the Fang. She guards the upper reaches of the caverns, ensuring that Naralex remains trapped in his corrupted sleep while dreaming of a reptilian future for the world.",["al"]={"what does anacondra do","lady anacondra purpose","why kill anacondra"},["q"]="What is her role in the Wailing Caverns?"},{["a"]="Lady Anacondra wanders the first large network of caverns near the entrance of the Wailing Caverns. She patrols among the cavern's raptors and serpents, often shifting between a few resting spots.",["al"]={"anacondra location","where is lady anacondra","anacondra spawn"},["q"]="Where can she be found inside the caverns?"},{["a"]="She carries the Gem of Anacondra. Slaying her and claiming the gem is required by the druid Nara Wildmane in Thunder Bluff to break the Fanglords' hold over the Barrens.",["al"]={"gem of anacondra","leaders of the fang anacondra","anacondra quest item"},["q"]="What item is taken from her for the Cenarion Circle?"},{["a"]="She draws upon nature magic, striking her foes from afar with searing bolts of lightning and casting magical slumber to incapacitate invaders while her reptilian allies attack.",["al"]={"anacondra abilities","anacondra spells","anacondra attacks"},["q"]="What powers does she wield in battle?"}},["kw"]={"anacondra","barrens","druids of the fang","fanglord","gem of anacondra","lady anacondra","naralex","scarletleaf","wailing caverns"},["n"]="Lady Anacondra",["s"]="Lady Anacondra is one of the Fanglords leading the Druids of the Fang within the Wailing Caverns. Once a night elf acolyte named Scarletleaf, she was the first to volunteer for Naralex's ambitious effort to heal the Barrens. When her master's Emerald Dream communion turned into a nightmare, her mind broke, twisting her devotion into a venomous drive to see Kalimdor overrun by serpents.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before adopting her serpentine title, Lady Anacondra was known as Scarletleaf. When the elder druid Naralex conceived of tapping into the subterranean springs of the Barrens through the Emerald Dream, she stepped forward as his very first volunteer. Her eager loyalty, however, proved her undoing. As Naralex's mind was seized by dark visions, the nightmare seeped out from the dreaming realm and contaminated his disciples, shattering Scarletleaf's sanity and reshaping her reverie into a cold, reptilian obsession.",["t"]="From Scarletleaf to Serpent"},{["b"]="Now styling herself Lady Anacondra, she stands guard among the first subterranean chambers of the Wailing Caverns. Like her fellow Fanglords, she abandoned the traditional tenets of the Cenarion Circle in favor of the vicious aspects of the viper. Channeling lightning, nature magic, and slumbering trances, she enforces Naralex's twisted slumber and works to spread the nightmare's corruption into the arid land above.",["t"]="A Fanglord in the Deep"}}}}}
t["npc:lady-sarevess"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,134,21.274.0,20.262.0,21.188.0,33.156.0,39.192.0",["h"]="1cf20c",["n"]="Lady Sarevess",["s"]="Lady Sarevess. Lady Sarevess es una retorcida hechicera naga que mora en las ruinas inundadas de Cavernas de Brazanegra, donde experimenta con oscuras brujerías. En la Alberca de Ask'ar, Lady Sarevess lleva a cabo sus rituales en una gruta inundada del templo en ruinas. Una taumaturga muy retorcida, experimenta con magia oscura mientras los cultores del Martillo Crepuscular que también rondan el templo sumergido continúan con su propio culto en lo más profundo de la caverna.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="Sarevess demonstrates how highborne magical practices degenerated into raw, chaotic lightning and tidal sorcery under centuries of oceanic corruption.",["race:NightElf"]="The ruins Lady Sarevess inhabits were once a sacred temple of Elune. Seeing her twisted naga kin defile the waters of Ask'ar is a bitter reminder of the Sundering."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Lady Sarevess is a naga spellcaster who has taken up residence within the subterranean Pool of Ask'ar inside Blackfathom Deeps. She is a very twisted spellcaster who dabbles in dark magic.",["al"]={"who is sarevess","sarevess lore","lady sarevess backstory"},["q"]="Who is Lady Sarevess?"},{["a"]="She makes her lair in the Pool of Ask'ar, a flooded chamber situated in the early reaches of the Blackfathom Deeps temple complex along the Ashenvale coast.",["al"]={"sarevess location","where is lady sarevess","pool of askar"},["q"]="Where can Lady Sarevess be found?"},{["a"]="Drawing upon the traditions of naga sea witches, Sarevess wields powerful water and elemental magic, particularly violent bursts of forked lightning, to strike down anyone who enters her cove.",["al"]={"sarevess magic","sarevess abilities"},["q"]="What powers does Lady Sarevess command?"}},["kw"]={"aku'mai","blackfathom deeps","lady sarevess","naga","pool of ask'ar","sarevess","sea witch","twilight's hammer"},["n"]="Lady Sarevess",["s"]="Lady Sarevess is a twisted naga sorceress dwelling within the flooded ruins of Blackfathom Deeps, where she dabbles in dark sorceries.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Within the Pool of Ask'ar, Lady Sarevess conducts her rituals in a flooded grotto of the ruined temple. A very twisted spellcaster, she dabbles in dark magic while the Twilight's Hammer cultists who also haunt the sunken temple pursue their own worship deeper in the cavern.",["t"]="A Grotto in the Deeps"},{["b"]="Much like a sea witch of the deep oceans, Sarevess commands elemental currents and crackling arcs of lightning. Surrounded by loyal naga sentinels and summoned water elementals, she fiercely defends her sanctuary against any intruders who threaten her dark work.",["t"]="Sorcery of the Tides"}}}}}
t["npc:laurna-morninglight"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="19,383,19.397.0,28.400.0,37.141.0,33.165.0,35.158.0,27.162.0,46.168.0,52.66.0",["h"]="5c6c97",["n"]="Laurna Luzdelalba",["s"]="Laurna Luzdelalba. Laurna Luzdelalba es una instructora de sacerdotes elfa de la noche que reside en el tranquilo asentamiento de Dolanaar, en Teldrassil. Devota de las Hermanas de Elune, guía a los acólitos en ciernes procedentes de Cañada Umbría en los ritos espirituales y las gracias sanadoras de la Diosa de la Luna. Sus enseñanzas preparan a los jóvenes sacerdotes elfos de la noche para las crecientes amenazas que acechan las ramas del Árbol del Mundo. Situada entre las ramas de Dolanaar, Laurna Luzdelalba ejerce como una de las principales mentoras de los jóvenes sacerdotes que han completado sus ritos iniciales en Cañada Umbría. A medida que los nuevos iniciados se adentran en las extensiones más amplias de Teldrassil, les enseña a profundizar en su comunión con Elune, equilibrando la luz sanadora con los ritos defensivos necesarios para sobrevivir en una naturaleza cada vez más hostil.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Priest"]="For night elf priests arriving from Shadowglen, Laurna Morninglight is your first major mentor outside the starting vale, teaching foundational spells and guiding your early devotion to Elune.",["race:NightElf"]="Laurna embodies the traditional kaldorei devotion to the Moon Goddess, reminding adventurers that priestcraft in Teldrassil draws from Elune rather than the Holy Light."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Laurna Morninglight is stationed in the village of Dolanaar, located in the central reaches of Teldrassil just down the road from Shadowglen.",["al"]={"laurna location","where is laurna","dolanaar priest trainer"},["q"]="Where can I find Laurna Morninglight?"},{["a"]="She is a priest trainer for night elf characters. She teaches new spells, refines ranks of known abilities, and provides early guidance through class-specific rites.",["al"]={"what does she do","laurna role","laurna priest trainer"},["q"]="What does Laurna Morninglight do?"},{["a"]="She initiates class quests for fledgling priests, directing them to aid wounded allies and seek Elune's divine favor through ceremonial vestments and prayers.",["al"]={"laurna quests","priest quests dolanaar"},["q"]="What kind of quests does she offer?"},{["a"]="While she is culturally rooted in the Sisterhood of Elune, priest trainers in the Alliance will instruct any allied priest who comes seeking spiritual discipline.",["al"]={"can humans train here","priest trainer any race"},["q"]="Does she train other races?"},{["a"]="Yes, as a kaldorei priestess, her vows and magic are dedicated entirely to the Goddess Elune and the broader traditions overseen by the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus.",["al"]={"is she sisterhood of elune","laurna temple of the moon"},["q"]="Is she affiliated with the Temple of the Moon?"},{["a"]="No relatives of Laurna are known among the kaldorei of Teldrassil.",["al"]={"morninglight family","laurna relatives"},["q"]="Does she share a family name with other night elves?"}},["kw"]={"dolanaar","elune","kaldorei","laurna","morninglight","priest trainer","sisterhood of elune","teldrassil"},["n"]="Laurna Morninglight",["s"]="Laurna Morninglight is a night elf priest trainer residing in the tranquil settlement of Dolanaar within Teldrassil. Devoted to the Sisterhood of Elune, she guides budding acolytes emerging from Shadowglen in the spiritual rites and healing graces of the Moon Goddess. Her teachings prepare young night elf priests for the growing threats encroaching on the boughs of the World Tree.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated amidst the boughs of Dolanaar, Laurna Morninglight serves as one of the primary mentors for young priests who have completed their initial rites in Shadowglen. As new initiates step out into the broader reaches of Teldrassil, she instructs them on expanding their communion with Elune, balancing the light of healing with defensive rites necessary to survive an increasingly hostile wild.",["t"]="A Guide in Dolanaar"},{["b"]="Priestcraft among the kaldorei is deeply intertwined with the worship of Elune rather than the abstract Holy Light revered by humans and dwarves. Laurna tasks her students with spiritual labors such as receiving sacred robes and healing a wounded Sentinel. Through these traditions, acolytes learn that their powers are direct gifts of the Mother Moon, meant to preserve and mend the kaldorei people.",["t"]="Devotion to the Moon Goddess"}}}}}
t["npc:lieutenant-farren-orinelle"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="26,423,19.515.0,16.458.0,34.183.0,24.167.0,32.172.0,38.136.0,31.143.0,28.98.0",["h"]="ba5f40",["n"]="Teniente Farren Orinelle",["s"]="Teniente Farren Orinelle. El Teniente Farren Orinelle es un oficial del ejército de Ventormenta actualmente destinado en la posada de Costasur, en las Laderas de Trabalomas. Profundamente descontento con su puesto fronterizo, pasa la mayor parte del tiempo bebiendo mientras subcontrata sus obligaciones a los viajeros que pasan por allí. Su principal asignación militar es ocuparse de los múrlocs que invaden la costa, una tarea que delega con entusiasmo con la esperanza de conseguir un traslado de vuelta al sur. El Teniente Farren Orinelle no eligió Costasur. Enviado lejos de Ciudad de Ventormenta, el teniente considera que las costas húmedas y disputadas de Trabalomas son un descenso deplorable respecto a las comodidades civilizadas de la capital. En lugar de patrullar los campos o coordinar las defensas con su oficial al mando, el Alguacil Rutagrana, Orinelle prácticamente ha fijado su residencia permanente en el interior de la posada de Costasur. Pasa los días enfurruñado, bebiendo y soñando con una orden oficial de traslado que lo devuelva al sur.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance champions, Orinelle represents the disgruntled Southern troops holding a lonely Northern outpost, willing to offer coin and commendation to anyone handling his duties.",["race:Human"]="As a Stormwind soldier stuck far from Elwynn Forest, Orinelle's disdain for northern frontier duty highlights the rift between comfortable capital life and harsh overseas deployments."},["faq"]={{["a"]="He is an officer of the Stormwind military stationed in Southshore, a town in the Hillsbrad Foothills. He can be found drinking inside the Southshore inn, grumbling about his posting.",["al"]={"farren orinelle","who is orinelle","southshore lieutenant"},["q"]="Who is Lieutenant Farren Orinelle?"},{["a"]="He was transferred north from Stormwind City to bolster the local garrison and support Marshal Redpath. He thoroughly dislikes the assignment and longs to return home.",["al"]={"why is farren in southshore","orinelle transfer"},["q"]="Why is he in Southshore?"},{["a"]="Marshal Redpath ordered him to deal with the hostile murlocs infesting the Hillsbrad coast, though Orinelle prefers paying traveling mercenaries to do the fighting for him.",["al"]={"farren duty","orinelle mission","farren murlocs"},["q"]="What is his official assignment?"},{["a"]="No. Orinelle spends almost all of his time lingering by the inn's bar, reluctant to brave the muddy beaches or hostile elements outside.",["al"]={"where to find farren","farren location","orinelle inn"},["q"]="Does he ever leave the Southshore inn?"},{["a"]="He wants nothing more than to secure an official reassignment back to Stormwind City, away from the dangers and bleakness of Lordaeron's coast.",["al"]={"what does farren want","reassignment"},["q"]="What is Farren's ultimate goal?"},{["a"]="He reports to Marshal Redpath, who commands the Alliance military detachment defending Southshore.",["al"]={"farren superior","farren boss","who commands farren"},["q"]="Who is Orinelle's commander?"}},["kw"]={"farren","hillsbrad","marshal redpath","murloc","orinelle","reassignment","southshore","stormwind"},["n"]="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle",["s"]="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle is an officer of the Stormwind army currently stationed at the Southshore inn in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Deeply unhappy with his frontier posting, he spends most of his time drinking while outsourcing his duties to passing travelers. His primary military assignment is dealing with the encroaching murlocs along the coast, a chore he eagerly delegates in hopes of securing a transfer back south.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle did not choose Southshore. Dispatched far from Stormwind City, the lieutenant finds the damp, contested shores of Hillsbrad a miserable step down from the civilized comforts of the capital. Instead of patrolling the fields or coordinating defenses with his commanding officer, Marshal Redpath, Orinelle has practically taken up permanent residence inside Southshore's inn. His days are spent sulking, drinking, and dreaming of an official transfer order that will return him to the south.",["t"]="Exile in Southshore"},{["b"]="Despite his comfortable seat at the tavern, Orinelle still answers to Marshal Redpath, who tasked the lieutenant with clearing out the murlocs swarming the nearby shoreline. Unwilling to soil his boots in coastal mud, Orinelle relies on wandering adventurers to cull the creatures and gather proof of their demise. He hopes that presenting tangible results back to his superiors will show his duty is accomplished, hastening his eventual recall to Stormwind.",["t"]="Outsourcing Duty"}}}}}
t["npc:lord-cobrahn"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="12,399,27.496.0,21.465.0,43.193.0,30.242.0,32.184.0,38.209.0,44.186.0,55.218.0",["h"]="feb6b4",["n"]="Lord Cobrahn",["s"]="Lord Cobrahn. Lord Cobrahn, anteriormente el druida elfo de la noche Jarlaxla, es uno de los corruptos Druidas del Colmillo que acechan en las profundidades de las Cuevas de los Lamentos. Antaño célebre en el Círculo Cenarion por su maestría con el cambio de forma, sucumbió a la pesadilla que infecta los manantiales de la caverna. Tras rebautizarse con el nombre de su nueva y letal apariencia, Cobrahn comanda ahora camadas de serpientes descarriadas y defiende el retorcido laberinto. Antes de adoptar el sobrenombre de Lord Cobrahn, Jarlaxla era un respetado miembro del Círculo Cenarion, elogiado entre sus compañeros druidas por su extraordinaria habilidad para canalizar formas animales. Cuando Naralex se adentró en las Cuevas de los Lamentos bajo Los Baldíos con la esperanza de aprovechar sus manantiales subterráneos y devolver una vida exuberante a los páramos áridos, Jarlaxla lo acompañó. Sin embargo, cuando la comunión de Naralex con el Sueño Esmeralda degeneró en una pesadilla retorcida, la mente de Jarlaxla se quebró junto a la de sus hermanos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Cobrahn serves as a grim warning of how druidic shapeshifting can be perverted when connected to the nightmare rather than natural balance.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde adventurers seek Cobrahn to end the foul corruption leaking into the Barrens and protect the fragile ecosystem of Kalimdor's plains.",["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, Cobrahn's fall is a bitter tragedy, seeing a skilled brother of the Cenarion Circle abandon his heritage to lead monsters in the subterranean depths."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Lord Cobrahn was originally named Jarlaxla. He was a prominent night elf druid within the Cenarion Circle, widely respected for his rare talent and deep affinity for animal shapeshifting forms.",["al"]={"cobrahn real name","who is cobrahn","jarlaxla"},["q"]="Who was Lord Cobrahn before he turned evil?"},{["a"]="Upon falling victim to the nightmare in the Wailing Caverns, Jarlaxla perfected a lethal serpentine shapeshifting form. He discarded his former name and took the title Lord Cobrahn to reflect his dangerous new power and mastery over serpents.",["al"]={"why cobrahn","lord cobrahn name meaning"},["q"]="Why is he called Lord Cobrahn?"},{["a"]="Lord Cobrahn resides deep within the Wailing Caverns, a twisting underground network located in the central Barrens, surrounded by deviate pythons and other nightmare-corrupted beasts.",["al"]={"cobrahn location","where is lord cobrahn","cobrahn room"},["q"]="Where can Lord Cobrahn be found?"},{["a"]="He is one of the primary Fanglords leading the Druids of the Fang. He carries the Gem of Cobrahn, which the druid Nara Wildmane of Thunder Bluff seeks in order to break the Fang leaders' hold over the Barrens.",["al"]={"why kill cobrahn","leaders of the fang cobrahn"},["q"]="Why do adventurers need to defeat him?"},{["a"]="Unlike ordinary night elves, Cobrahn is noticeably larger in stature, wields a sharp claw on his right hand, and can transform completely into an oversized, venomous snake during combat.",["al"]={"what does cobrahn look like","cobrahn appearance"},["q"]="What unique physical traits does he possess?"},{["a"]="Cobrahn is one of the four key Fanglords alongside Lady Anacondra and their kin. They are former Cenarion Circle druids who entered the caverns with Naralex and jointly fell to the twisting corruption of the nightmare.",["al"]={"druids of the fang leaders","cobrahn and anacondra"},["q"]="What is his connection to the other Druids of the Fang?"}},["kw"]={"cobrahn","deviate python","druids of the fang","fanglord","gem of cobrahn","jarlaxla","lord cobrahn","wailing caverns"},["n"]="Lord Cobrahn",["s"]="Lord Cobrahn, formerly the night elf druid Jarlaxla, is one of the corrupted Druids of the Fang lurking deep within the Wailing Caverns. Once renowned within the Cenarion Circle for his mastery of shapeshifting, he succumbed to the nightmare infecting the cavern springs. Renaming himself after his new lethal guise, Cobrahn now commands broods of deviate serpents and defends the twisted labyrinth.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before adopting the moniker Lord Cobrahn, Jarlaxla was a respected member of the Cenarion Circle, celebrated among his fellow druids for his extraordinary skill in channeling animal forms. When Naralex ventured into the Wailing Caverns beneath the Barrens hoping to tap their underground springs and restore lush life to the arid wastes, Jarlaxla accompanied him. However, when Naralex's Emerald Dream communion decayed into a twisting nightmare, Jarlaxla's mind shattered alongside his brothers.",["t"]="A Master of Forms Corrupted"},{["b"]="Rather than channeling the traditional totemic beasts of Cenarion tradition, the nightmare warped Jarlaxla's shapeshifting prowess into something predatory and reptilian. Adopting the name Lord Cobrahn, he developed a deadly serpentine form that he unleashes in battle. Flanked by venomous deviate pythons and bearing a vicious clawed right hand, he oversees his section of the grottos, violently purging anyone seeking to break the nightmare's hold on the caverns.",["t"]="The Serpent's Embrace"}}}}}
t["npc:lord-ello-ebonlocke"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="19,289,19.500.0,18.576.0,29.465.1,27.208.0,48.218.0,59.294.0,39.106.0,57.276.0,54.125.1",["h"]="ee89ed",["n"]="Lord Ello Cerranegro",["s"]="Lord Ello Cerranegro. Lord Ello Cerranegro es el alcalde de Villa Oscura y el líder de su consejo de gobierno, apostado en el ayuntamiento de Villa Oscura. Rodeado por la oscuridad y horrores acechantes, lucha a diario por mantener el orden y proteger a sus asediados ciudadanos a pesar de recibir escasa ayuda de Ventormenta. Sentado en la penumbra del ayuntamiento de Villa Oscura, Lord Ello Cerranegro carga con el pesado fardo de gobernar un asentamiento al borde de la ruina. Antaño parte del próspero remanso rural conocido como Grand Hamlet, Villa Oscura se encuentra ahora asfixiada por una sombra perpetua y asediada por necrófagos voraces, abominaciones esqueléticas y bestias salvajes. Ello preside el Consejo de Villa Oscura, esforzándose contra viento y marea por mantener en funcionamiento los vestigios de la civilización mientras Ventormenta hace la vista gorda ante su difícil situación.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,1},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Lord Ebonlocke represents the forgotten edges of the Alliance, where isolated mayors must lead their people through nightmare conditions without imperial aid.",["race:Human"]="For humans traveling from Stormwind, speaking with Lord Ebonlocke is a sobering reminder of how far the southern provinces have fallen into ruin and abandonment."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Lord Ello Ebonlocke is the mayor of Darkshire and head of the Council of Darkshire. From his seat in the town hall, he oversees the defense, civic affairs, and survival of Duskwood's remaining human populace.",["al"]={"who is ello","mayor of darkshire","ello ebonlocke lore"},["q"]="Who is Lord Ello Ebonlocke?"},{["a"]="Commander Althea Ebonlocke, the stalwart leader of the Night Watch, is Lord Ello's close kin. While he governs the civic and diplomatic affairs of Darkshire, she directs the militia that actively guards the settlement.",["al"]={"althea ebonlocke relation","is althea ello's daughter"},["q"]="How is he related to Commander Althea Ebonlocke?"},{["a"]="When Magistrate Solomon requests aid against the Blackrock orcs in Redridge, Lord Ebonlocke is forced to refuse. Darkshire is so hard-pressed by undead and monstrosities that stripping the town of guards would cause it to be completely overrun before the militia even reached the forest border.",["al"]={"why no help for redridge","messenger to darkshire","magistrate solomon ello ebonlocke"},["q"]="Why does Lord Ebonlocke refuse to send troops to Lakeshire?"},{["a"]="He is located inside the Darkshire Town Hall, which stands at the center of Darkshire in eastern Duskwood.",["al"]={"ello ebonlocke location","where is mayor ebonlocke"},["q"]="Where can Lord Ello Ebonlocke be found?"},{["a"]="Stormwind is embroiled in internal political strife following King Varian Wrynn's disappearance. With the kingdom's resources constrained, the House of Nobles has largely abandoned the southern regions, forcing local leaders like Lord Ebonlocke to organize their own defenses.",["al"]={"why won't stormwind help duskwood","stormwind neglect"},["q"]="Why doesn't Stormwind send troops to help Lord Ebonlocke?"},{["a"]="Lord Ebonlocke assists in handling communications with the hermit Abercrombie, helping arrange translations of strange notes.",["al"]={"ello abercrombie note","translate abercrombie's note"},["q"]="What is Lord Ebonlocke's involvement with Abercrombie?"}},["kw"]={"abercrombie","althea","council","darkshire","duskwood","ebonlocke","ello","lakeshire","mayor"},["n"]="Lord Ello Ebonlocke",["s"]="Lord Ello Ebonlocke is the mayor of Darkshire and the leader of its governing council, stationed inside the Darkshire Town Hall. Surrounded by darkness and creeping horrors, he struggles daily to maintain order and protect his besieged citizens despite receiving little aid from Stormwind.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Seated in the gloom of the Darkshire Town Hall, Lord Ello Ebonlocke bears the heavy burden of governing a settlement on the brink of ruin. Once part of the prosperous rural haven known as Grand Hamlet, Darkshire is now smothered by perpetual shadow and besieged by ravenous ghouls, skeletal abominations, and feral beasts. Ello presides over the Council of Darkshire, striving against impossible odds to keep the remnants of civilization functioning while Stormwind turns a blind eye to their plight.",["t"]="A Beleaguered Mayor"},{["b"]="Because Stormwind's garrison refuses to spare soldiers for the borderlands, Darkshire relies almost entirely on local volunteer militias like the Night Watch, commanded by his relative, Althea Ebonlocke. When neighboring leaders like Magistrate Solomon of Lakeshire plead for reinforcements to combat Blackrock orcs, Lord Ebonlocke must make agonizing choices. As he solemnly explains to messengers from Redridge, Darkshire cannot spare a single blade: sending their guards beyond the forest's edge would leave their own homes to be instantly overrun by the surrounding evils.",["t"]="A Divided Frontier"},{["b"]="Beyond patrolling the roads, Lord Ebonlocke frequently relies on wandering adventurers to handle peculiar matters around the woods. In his earnest desire to assist all residents of Duskwood, he coordinates communications with solitary figures like the hermit Abercrombie. Regrettably, Ebonlocke's lack of true insight into the hermit's cryptic writings blinds him to the grisly, stitched nightmare festering just beyond the town borders until it is nearly too late.",["t"]="Blind to the Hermit's Designs"}}}}}
t["npc:lord-pythas"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="11,387,16.558.0,19.501.0,19.193.0,32.286.0,56.259.0,38.253.0,31.132.0,24.228.0",["h"]="523b4e",["n"]="Lord Pythas",["s"]="Lord Pythas. Lord Pythas, antaño un guerrero elfo de la noche llamado Aryn, es uno de los cuatro líderes corruptos de los Druidas del Colmillo en las Cuevas de los Lamentos. En su origen amigo de la infancia y protector jurado del archidruida Naralex, cayó víctima de la pesadilla que contamina el oasis subterráneo. Ahora blande tanto poder marcial como una retorcida magia de serpiente contra cualquiera que intente llegar hasta su aletargado maestro. Antes de adoptar el sobrenombre de Pythas, este elfo de la noche era conocido como Aryn. Un curtido guerrero y leal compañero de infancia de Naralex, sirvió como guardia personal del archidruida cuando la expedición se adentró en los secarrales de Los Baldíos. Deseoso de servir mejor al ambicioso sueño de Naralex de restaurar la frondosa vida en el árido reino, Aryn comenzó a estudiar el druidismo y demostró un aprendizaje excepcionalmente rápido. Sin embargo, la disciplina física y el valor marcial no ofrecieron protección alguna contra la insidiosa corrupción que aguardaba en lo profundo de las fisuras subterráneas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Pythas represents the tragic fate of a promising acolyte who embraced nature magic out of devotion, only to have the Emerald Dream's corruption twist his teachings into a viperous heresy.",["class:Warrior"]="Before he was corrupted into a serpent cultist, Pythas was a disciplined night elf warrior and personal protector—a grim reminder that martial prowess alone cannot stave off mental madness.",["race:NightElf"]="Watching a respected protector like Aryn fall to dark madness is a bitter sorrow for any night elf seeking to restore balance to the scarred soils of Kalimdor."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Lord Pythas was originally a night elf warrior named Aryn. He was a childhood friend and personal bodyguard to Archdruid Naralex who studied druidism to assist his master's work in the Barrens.",["al"]={"who is pythas","lord pythas lore","who was aryn"},["q"]="Who is Lord Pythas?"},{["a"]="Pythas did not betray Naralex willingly. When Naralex attempted to tap into the Emerald Dream to heal the Barrens, a nightmare seized the archdruid's thoughts. The corrupting dream seeped into the minds of his acolytes, stripping away Aryn's sanity and remaking him into a serpent lord.",["al"]={"why is pythas evil","how did pythas go mad","why did he become druid of the fang"},["q"]="Why did he turn against Naralex?"},{["a"]="Unlike the other leaders who rely purely on nature magic and beast forms, Pythas was a seasoned warrior before training as a druid. He combines martial combat skill with druidic magic, making him one of the most physically formidable defenders in the caverns.",["al"]={"pythas fighting style","pythas vs other leaders"},["q"]="What makes Pythas different from the other Fang leaders?"},{["a"]="Pythas carries one of the four enchanted gems needed to complete the quest Leaders of the Fang. The quest is given by the druid Nara Wildmane in Thunder Bluff, who requires the gems of all four Fang leaders to free the Barrens from their twisted dreams.",["al"]={"leaders of the fang quest","gem of pythas"},["q"]="Why do adventurers need to defeat him?"},{["a"]="Lord Pythas lurks within the deep interior chambers of the Wailing Caverns, surrounded by corrupted beasts and fellow Fang cultists.",["al"]={"pythas location","where is pythas"},["q"]="Where can Lord Pythas be found?"},{["a"]="Upon his defeat, the Gem of Pythas is recovered from his remains. Adventurers bring it, along with the gems of the other three serpent lords, to Nara Wildmane in Thunder Bluff to prove the leadership of the Fang has been broken.",["al"]={"gem of pythas use","what is gem of pythas"},["q"]="What happens to his gem?"}},["kw"]={"aryn","druids of the fang","gem of pythas","leaders of the fang","lord pythas","naralex","pythas","wailing caverns"},["n"]="Lord Pythas",["s"]="Lord Pythas, once a night elf warrior named Aryn, is one of the four corrupted leaders of the Druids of the Fang in the Wailing Caverns. Originally a childhood friend and sworn protector of the archdruid Naralex, he fell victim to the nightmare tainting the oasis underground. Now he wields both martial might and twisted serpent magic against any who try to reach his slumbering master.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before adopting the moniker Pythas, this night elf was known as Aryn. A seasoned warrior and trusted childhood companion to Naralex, he served as the archdruid's personal guard when the expedition ventured into the dry wastes of the Barrens. Eager to better serve Naralex's ambitious dream of restoring lush life to the arid realm, Aryn took up the study of druidism, proving to be an exceptionally fast learner. However, physical discipline and martial valor offered no shelter against the insidious corruption waiting deep within the subterranean fissures.",["t"]="A Guardian Falls"},{["b"]="When Naralex's connection to the Emerald Dream was hijacked by dark nightmares, Aryn's mind succumbed alongside those of his fellow acolytes. Shedding his former name and loyalty, he became Lord Pythas, leader among the Druids of the Fang. Where his fellow serpent lords favor cunning spellcasting or beast forms, Pythas seamlessly blends lethal combat prowess with nature magic. He now prowls the winding tunnels of the caverns, determined to defend the nightmare's twisted grip on the cavern spring.",["t"]="The Lethal Sentinel"}}}}}
t["npc:lord-serpentis"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,426,32.350.0,18.412.0,18.316.1,22.250.0,28.208.0,36.242.0,32.234.0,31.285.0",["h"]="f2d928",["n"]="Lord Serpentis",["s"]="Lord Serpentis. Lord Serpentis es un druida elfo de la noche corrupto que se erige como uno de los cuatro líderes de los renegados Druidas del Colmillo dentro de las Cuevas de los Lamentos. Antaño un druida de gran poder y prestigio en la orden de Naralex, cayó en la locura cuando el sueño de Naralex se convirtió en una pesadilla dentro de los manantiales subterráneos. Ahora, ayuda a liderar la secta que rinde culto a las serpientes en las profundidades de las cavernas, donde el corrupto Naralex yace aletargado. Antes de que la oscuridad se apoderara de los manantiales de la caverna, Serpentis era un druida de gran poder y prestigio, miembro de la noble orden liderada por Naralex que esperaba utilizar los manantiales de las cavernas y el Sueño Esmeralda para sanar Los Baldíos. Sin embargo, cuando la visión de Naralex se convirtió en una pesadilla corruptora, Serpentis estuvo entre los druidas cuyas mentes sucumbieron a la locura emergente.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Serpentis represents the tragic danger lurking within the Emerald Dream, showcasing how even a druid of great power can be twisted when a noble vision becomes a nightmare.",["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, Serpentis and his followers are a painful disgrace—kaldorei scholars of great renown who threw away their sacred duty to nature to become monstrous serpent lords.",["race:Tauren"]="Tauren see the corruption of Serpentis as a foul desecration of the Earth Mother's balance, threatening the fragile ecosystem of the Barrens with unnatural madness."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Lord Serpentis is one of the four leaders of the Druids of the Fang, located deep within the Wailing Caverns. Once a night elf druid of great power and prestige in Naralex's order, he was corrupted by Naralex's nightmare along with his fellow druids.",["al"]={"who is serpentis","lord serpentis lore","serpentis background"},["q"]="Who is Lord Serpentis?"},{["a"]="When Naralex's attempt to heal the Barrens through the Emerald Dream turned into a nightmare, its corruption spread to the druids who followed him, turning Serpentis's mind toward madness and serpent worship.",["al"]={"why did serpentis turn","serpentis corruption","why is serpentis bad"},["q"]="Why did Serpentis turn evil?"},{["a"]="Serpentis was once one of the noble druids who followed Naralex into the caverns. Rather than aiding in his master's recovery, he became a leader of the Druids of the Fang, who now seek to remake the Barrens to match their own twisted dreams.",["al"]={"serpentis and naralex","is serpentis related to naralex","naralex apprentice"},["q"]="What is his relationship to Naralex?"},{["a"]="Serpentis is one of the four leaders of the Druids of the Fang. Eliminating him is essential to break the sect's grip on the Wailing Caverns, secure his gem for the quest Leaders of the Fang, and clear a path toward awakening Naralex.",["al"]={"why kill serpentis","leaders of the fang serpentis","gem of serpentis"},["q"]="Why do players need to kill him?"},{["a"]="They are a renegade faction of night elf druids who followed Naralex into the Wailing Caverns. Corrupted by the Emerald Nightmare, they abandoned traditional druidic forms to adopt the aspects, venoms, and behaviors of serpents under the command of Serpentis and their other fanglords.",["al"]={"druids of the fang lore","what are druids of the fang","fang druids"},["q"]="Who are the Druids of the Fang?"}},["kw"]={"druids of the fang","gem of serpentis","leaders of the fang","lord serpentis","naralex","serpentis","wailing caverns"},["n"]="Lord Serpentis",["s"]="Lord Serpentis is a corrupted night elf druid who stands as one of the four leaders of the rogue Druids of the Fang within the Wailing Caverns. Once a druid of great power and prestige in the order of Naralex, he was twisted into madness when Naralex's dream became a nightmare within the subterranean springs. Now, he helps command the serpent-worshipping sect deep in the caverns where the corrupted Naralex lies slumbering.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before darkness overtook the cavern springs, Serpentis was a druid of great power and prestige, one of the noble order led by Naralex that hoped to use the caverns' springs and the Emerald Dream to heal the Barrens. However, when Naralex's vision became a corrupting nightmare, Serpentis was among the druids whose minds fell to the emerging madness.",["t"]="From Noble Druid to Serpent Lord"},{["b"]="Succumbing completely to the corruption radiating from Naralex's twisted dreams, Serpentis and his fellow druids became the Druids of the Fang. Forsaking traditional Cenarion balance and the totem animals of old, they now seek to remake the Barrens to match their own twisted dreams rather than heal it. Serpentis rules the sect as one of its four leaders, alongside Lady Anacondra, Lord Cobrahn and Lord Pythas.",["t"]="A Lord of the Fang"},{["b"]="Perched deep inside the winding caverns, Lord Serpentis is one of the four leaders of the rogue sect, each of whom carries a dream gem. Those seeking to wake the trapped master or reclaim the waters of the Oasis must strike down Serpentis and claim the gem he carries, breaking the serpent's hold over the labyrinth.",["t"]="The Final Obstacle"}}}}}
t["npc:lorgus-jett"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="11,350,22.373.0,26.480.0,19.179.0,52.199.0,41.223.0,26.202.0,40.200.0,45.198.0",["h"]="51b889",["n"]="Lorgus Jett",["s"]="Lorgus Jett. Lorgus Jett es un miembro humano del culto del Martillo Crepuscular que opera en los pasillos inundados de las Cavernas de Brazanegra. Mientras vaga por las Ruinas del Santuario Lunar, actúa como un despiadado comandante al servicio del culto a los dioses antiguos. Los líderes de la Horda lo han señalado como un objetivo prioritario para frenar el avance del culto a lo largo de la costa de Vallefresno. Aunque muchos miembros del Martillo Crepuscular que operan bajo las Cavernas de Brazanegra provienen de linajes orcos o tauren, Lorgus Jett destaca por ser un humano en los rincones más profundos de unas antiguas ruinas de elfos de la noche. Vagando por cualquier lugar entre las Ruinas del Santuario Lunar superiores y los túneles cavernosos más allá del profanador múrloc Gelihast, Jett coordina los oscuros rituales y las violentas ambiciones del culto.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Paladin"]="Lorgus Jett represents a horrifying warning to the Silver Hand: a former brother who abandoned the Light's tenets to embrace the mad prophecies of the Old Gods.",["class:Shaman"]="Jett wields the elements not in harmony or reverence, but through the corrupted, violent methods taught by the Twilight's Hammer.",["faction:Horde"]="Striking down Lorgus Jett fulfills an urgent request to sever the leadership of the Twilight's Hammer festering beneath the Ashenvale shore.",["race:Human"]="Seeing a human so far west in Kalimdor serving cosmic terrors is a chilling reminder of how far the corruption of the Twilight's Hammer has reached."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Lorgus Jett is a human operative of the Twilight's Hammer cult stationed inside Blackfathom Deeps. He oversees cult activities within the Moonshrine Ruins and serves the Old Gods.",["al"]={"lorgus jett lore","who is lorgus","lorgus jett background"},["q"]="Who is Lorgus Jett?"},{["a"]="Lorgus Jett has a variable patrol area within the Moonshrine Ruins. He can appear near the earliest clusters of Twilight cultists or farther along in the flooded passages just past Gelihast's shrine.",["al"]={"lorgus jett location","where is lorgus jett","find lorgus jett"},["q"]="Where can Lorgus Jett be found in Blackfathom Deeps?"},{["a"]="The Horde seeks his death through the mission 'Allegiance to the Old Gods.' His presence in Ashenvale threatens regional stability and represents an insidious alliance dedicated to unleashing ancient, world-ending entities.",["al"]={"why kill lorgus","allegiance to the old gods quest"},["q"]="Why does the Horde want Lorgus Jett dead?"},{["a"]="Relics associated with him—such as discarded tenets of the Silver Hand and paladin armor—strongly indicate he was once a holy knight of the Silver Hand who renounced the Light to serve the Old Gods.",["al"]={"lorgus jett silver hand","is lorgus a fallen paladin"},["q"]="Was Lorgus Jett a paladin?"},{["a"]="The Twilight's Hammer communes directly with chaotic elemental forces and Old Gods rather than traditional ancestral spirits, allowing non-traditional races like humans to wield elemental devastation.",["al"]={"lorgus jett magic","human shaman lorgus"},["q"]="Why does a human use shamanistic powers?"},{["a"]="Both dwell in the Moonshrine Ruins of Blackfathom Deeps, united in their servitude to the dark powers sleeping beneath the sea, with Jett frequently patrolling the corridors beyond Gelihast's altar.",["al"]={"lorgus and gelihast","gelihast connection"},["q"]="What is Lorgus Jett's connection to Gelihast?"}},["kw"]={"allegiance to the old gods","blackfathom deeps","fallen paladin","lorgus jett","moonshrine ruins","silver hand","twilight's hammer"},["n"]="Lorgus Jett",["s"]="Lorgus Jett is a human member of the Twilight's Hammer cult operating within the flooded corridors of Blackfathom Deeps. Wandering the Moonshrine Ruins, he serves as a ruthless commander in the cult's service to the Old Gods. Horde leaders have singled him out as a primary target to disrupt the cult's encroaching presence along the Ashenvale coast.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While many members of the Twilight's Hammer working under Blackfathom Deeps hail from orcish or tauren lineages, Lorgus Jett stands out as a human in the deep recesses of ancient night elf ruins. Roaming anywhere between the upper Moonshrine Ruins and the cavernous tunnels beyond the murloc defiler Gelihast, Jett coordinates the cult's dark rituals and violent ambitions.",["t"]="A Defiler in the Ruins"},{["b"]="Though he wields elemental incantations uncommon among humanity, Jett carries relics that hint at a darker past. Scattered among his possessions are discarded tenets and armor bearing the mark of the Knights of the Silver Hand, alongside a massive hammer forged for righteous judgment. His presence suggests that even the devout holy warriors of the Eastern Kingdoms can succumb to the maddening whispers of the Old Gods, casting aside holy vows in exchange for apocalyptic power.",["t"]="Shadows of the Silver Hand"}}}}}
t["npc:madame-eva"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="10,372,31.351.0,26.353.0,36.319.0,18.177.0,52.237.0,32.252.0,42.149.0,35.178.0,50.201.0",["h"]="ec871c",["n"]="Lady Eva",["s"]="Lady Eva. Lady Eva es una venerada adivina y matriarca que vive en Villa Oscura, en el sombrío Bosque del Ocaso. Practicante de antiguas artes místicas de adivinación y cartomancia, a menudo es la primera lugareña en percibir perturbaciones antinaturales por todo el bosque. Los viajeros acuden con frecuencia a ella para desentrañar lúgubres misterios o conseguir talismanes ocultos contra la oscuridad que acecha. Lady Eva, que vive discretamente entre las sombras de Villa Oscura, practica la cartomancia y antiguos rituales populares que muchos en la catedral de Ventormenta verían con recelo. En una región olvidada y asolada por bestias salvajes, no-muertos y horrores aún más oscuros, sus inquietantes visiones son toleradas y buscadas tanto por los desesperados lugareños como por los aventureros de paso.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Priest"]="While the Holy Light brings solace to the living, priests will find Eva's reliance on cartomancy and spirit remnants a curious, earthen counterpoint to traditional church liturgy.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance champions stepping into the oppressive shadow of Duskwood, Madame Eva is an indispensable guide whose premonitions cut through the woods' deadly confusion.",["profession:Tailoring"]="Tailors will appreciate Eva's knowledge of bizarre weaving materials, specifically her ability to work spectral thread plucked directly from the ghosts of the region."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Madame Eva is an elderly human fortune-teller and diviner residing in Darkshire. She practices cartomancy and ancient folk crafts to glimpse the unseen perils stalking Duskwood.",["al"]={"madame eva","who is eva","darkshire fortune teller"},["q"]="Who is Madame Eva?"},{["a"]="Madame Eva reads the cards and senses an imminent, supernatural danger encircling her granddaughter Alyssa. Her readings guide adventurers to investigate forgotten documents and trails that uncover the grim history of Stalvan Mistmantle.",["al"]={"eva stalvan","legend of stalvan eva","why does eva care about stalvan"},["q"]="What is Madame Eva's role in the mystery of Stalvan?"},{["a"]="Eva is primarily a seer and practitioner of older mystic arts, such as cartomancy, spirit-thread weaving, and folk effigies. Her magic is more akin to traditional fortune-telling and occult lore than the structured arcanum of Dalaran or the Holy Light.",["al"]={"is eva a witch","eva magic type","what magic does eva use"},["q"]="Is Madame Eva a witch or a mage?"},{["a"]="She is the grandmother of Alyssa Eva and Lohgan Eva. The town's Night Watch also includes Watcher Eva, who is believed to share ties with her family.",["al"]={"eva family","madame eva grandchildren","alyssa eva grandmother"},["q"]="Who is related to Madame Eva in Darkshire?"},{["a"]="Madame Eva gathers ethereal strands of ghost hair thread from restless spirits to weave specially prepared ritual garments and provide supplies needed by allies across the realm.",["al"]={"ghost hair thread","eva thread quest"},["q"]="What is Ghost Hair Thread used for?"},{["a"]="Madame Eva crafts the Totem of Infliction as a dark, sympathetic effigy. By binding specific creature materials to it, the totem directs curses and harm back onto the fell beasts terrorizing the woods.",["al"]={"totem of infliction","eva totem"},["q"]="Why does Madame Eva craft the Totem of Infliction?"}},["kw"]={"alyssa eva","cartomancy","darkshire","duskwood","fortune teller","ghost hair thread","madame eva","stalvan"},["n"]="Madame Eva",["s"]="Madame Eva is a revered fortune-teller and matriarch living in Darkshire in the shadowed forest of Duskwood. Practicing older, mystic arts of divination and cartomancy, she often serves as the first townsperson to sense unnatural disturbances across the woods. Travelers frequently seek her out to unravel grim mysteries or procure occult charms against the creeping dark.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Dwelling quietly amidst the gloom of Darkshire, Madame Eva practices cartomancy and ancient folk rituals that many in Stormwind's cathedral would view with suspicion. In a forsaken region plagued by feral beasts, the undead, and darker horrors, her eerie insights are tolerated and sought after by desperate townspeople and visiting adventurers alike.",["t"]="The Fortune-Teller of Darkshire"},{["b"]="Beyond her role as an occult reader, Madame Eva is deeply devoted to her family, serving as grandmother to Alyssa Eva and young Lohgan. When her cartomancy reveals dark omens threatening her granddaughter, Eva does not hesitate to enlist the aid of passing wanderers to scour the woods, uncovering long-buried tragedies before history can repeat itself.",["t"]="Ties of Blood and Prophecy"},{["b"]="Eva's knowledge extends beyond card reading to ritual crafting and warding. From weaving supernatural garments using spectral thread to crafting bizarre folk relics like the Totem of Infliction, she understands the strange, twilight logic that governs Duskwood's restless spirits better than almost anyone else in town.",["t"]="Weaving Protection Against the Night"}}}}}
t["npc:magatha-grimtotem"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,243,27.449.0,18.431.0,22.412.1,25.284.0,38.301.0,53.256.0,39.270.0,15.251.0,37.140.0",["h"]="7a37f2",["n"]="Magatha Tótem Siniestro",["s"]="Magatha Tótem Siniestro. Magatha Tótem Siniestro es la matriarca de la tribu Tótem Siniestro y la vieja bruja de Cima del Trueno. Una formidable chamana e intrigante política, reside en el Alto de los Ancestros mientras desafía continuamente la visión de Cairne Pezuña de Sangre para la nación tauren. Magatha ascendió a la autoridad absoluta sobre los Tótem Siniestro a través de una unión concertada seguida del repentino y mortal accidente de escalada de su pareja. Operando desde el Alto de los Ancestros con su séquito personal y guardaespaldas, se erige como la líder política y espiritual indiscutible de su aislada tribu. A diferencia de Cairne Pezuña de Sangre, Magatha predica la dominación tauren, considerando a las otras razas mortales como intrusas en Kalimdor que deberían ser erradicadas o apartadas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Shaman"]="Magatha is undeniably one of the most powerful shamans on Kalimdor, commanding primal elements with an authority few living tauren can rival.",["faction:Horde"]="While Magatha offers valuable aid and council against regional threats, her fierce clan loyalty and open contempt for other races make her an untrustworthy comrade.",["race:Tauren"]="Every tauren knows of the Grimtotem's dark reputation, making Magatha's presence on Elder Rise an uneasy reminder of the ideological divide threatening their united tribes.",["race:Undead"]="Forsaken travelers find a surprisingly warm reception from the Elder Crone, who actively consults the Royal Apothecary Society in the Pools of Vision."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Magatha is the elder crone and matriarch of the Grimtotem tribe. A gifted shaman since childhood, she assumed total rule of her clan after her mate died in a climbing accident. She resides on Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff, where she serves as Cairne Bloodhoof's primary political rival.",["al"]={"magatha backstory","who is the elder crone","elder crone thunder bluff"},["q"]="Who is Magatha Grimtotem?"},{["a"]="Ostensibly, Magatha believes tauren traditions and shamanic understanding can guide the Forsaken back toward humanity. However, many suspect her friendship with the Royal Apothecary Society is driven by a desire for esoteric alchemical secrets and political allies outside Cairne's loyal inner circle.",["al"]={"magatha and undead","why magatha likes forsaken","magatha apothecary zamah"},["q"]="Why does Magatha support the Forsaken?"},{["a"]="Magatha views Cairne as soft, naive, and unfit to lead the united tauren. While Cairne advocates coexistence within the Horde and peace across Kalimdor, Magatha believes the Grimtotem should reclaim ancestral lands by force and eliminate foreign intruders.",["al"]={"magatha vs cairne","does magatha hate cairne","cairne and magatha"},["q"]="What is Magatha's relationship with Cairne Bloodhoof?"},{["a"]="Magatha sent an emissary named Maur into Ragefire Chasm beneath Orgrimmar to negotiate with the resident troggs. The troggs killed Maur instead, prompting Magatha to send Horde adventurers into the cavern to retrieve Maur's satchel and butcher the troggs in retribution.",["al"]={"magatha ragefire quest","why magatha sent maur","lost satchel magatha"},["q"]="What was the mission in Ragefire Chasm?"},{["a"]="Arikara is a vengeful wind serpent spirit said to seek retribution against the tauren people. Magatha claims Arikara seeks vengeance directly against Cairne Bloodhoof and tasks capable champions with using enchanted agave to summon and slay the beast.",["al"]={"serpent of vengeance","arikara quest","magatha arikara"},["q"]="Who is Arikara?"},{["a"]="Magatha resides inside the large main tent atop Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff, attended by her servant Rahauro and two stoic Grimtotem guards.",["al"]={"magatha location","where is magatha","magatha elder rise"},["q"]="Where can Magatha Grimtotem be found?"}},["kw"]={"arikara","bloodhoof","cairne","elder crone","elder rise","grimtotem","magatha","ragefire","thunder bluff","zamah"},["n"]="Magatha Grimtotem",["s"]="Magatha Grimtotem is the matriarch of the Grimtotem tribe and the Elder Crone of Thunder Bluff. A formidable shaman and political schemer, she resides on Elder Rise while continually challenging Cairne Bloodhoof's vision for the tauren nation.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Magatha rose to absolute authority over the Grimtotem through an arranged union followed by the sudden, fatal climbing accident of her mate. Operating from Elder Rise with her personal retinue and bodyguards, she stands as the undisputed political and spiritual leader of her reclusive tribe. Unlike Cairne Bloodhoof, Magatha preaches tauren dominance, viewing other mortal races as intruders upon Kalimdor who ought to be eradicated or swept aside.",["t"]="The Matriarch of Elder Rise"},{["b"]="Despite her open disdain for non-tauren, Magatha was among the earliest advocates for admitting the Forsaken into the Horde. She claims the tauren can teach the undead spiritual balance and guide them toward reclaiming their humanity. In practice, however, Magatha collaborates directly with the Royal Apothecary Society beneath Thunder Bluff, consulting figures like Apothecary Zamah on practical alchemy and arcane relic studies.",["t"]="A Curious Alliance"},{["b"]="Behind a facade of wise counsel, Magatha actively works to weaken Cairne's authority while testing the defenses of potential threats. She dispatches adventurers into deep hazards—from probing trogg forces in Ragefire Chasm to hunting down the vengeful spirit Arikara. Every task she assigns serves to either consolidate Grimtotem leverage or prepare for the day she can supplant the Bloodhoof dynasty entirely.",["t"]="Political Machinations"}}}}}
t["npc:maggran-earthbinder"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="19,387,17.455.0,20.472.0,27.247.0,41.256.0,55.228.0,44.210.0,42.201.0,52.133.0",["h"]="631ce7",["n"]="Ligaterra Maggran",["s"]="Ligaterra Maggran. Ligaterra Maggran es un veterano tauren entrado en años al que el gran jefe Cairne Pezuña de Sangre designó para liderar el campamento de la Horda en el Refugio Roca del Sol. Curtido por una vida entera de brutales conflictos, supervisa la defensa de los escarpados valles de Sierra Espolón frente a bestias voraces y agresivas parvadas de arpías. Aunque fatigado por incontables batallas, sigue siendo un guardián inquebrantable del asentamiento. Ligaterra Maggran fue enviado a Sierra Espolón por el mismísimo gran jefe Cairne Pezuña de Sangre. Como veterano de incontables escaramuzas y sangrientas campañas, Maggran admite que la edad y la violencia han endurecido su corazón, despojándolo de la apacibilidad natural característica de su pueblo. El Refugio Roca del Sol debía ser tanto un puesto avanzado bajo su firme mando como un lugar de sosiego, donde los vientos cálidos y el sol de la montaña pudieran aliviar su espíritu desgastado por la guerra.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="For travelers navigating the steep climbs of Stonetalon, Maggran is the primary authority coordinating local Horde patrols and keeping supply routes clear of beasts and harpies.",["race:Tauren"]="Maggran embodies the heavy toll warfare takes on the shu'halo spirit, serving as a reminder of how conflict can harden even the most grounded children of the Earth Mother."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Maggran Earthbinder is the commanding tauren elder at Sun Rock Retreat in the Stonetalon Mountains. Hardened by countless battles, he was stationed here by Cairne Bloodhoof to watch over the settlement and keep its supply roads and borders secure.",["al"]={"maggran","who is maggran","sun rock retreat leader"},["q"]="Who is Maggran Earthbinder?"},{["a"]="Cairne Bloodhoof appointed him to lead Sun Rock Retreat partly for his seasoned military leadership and partly as a retreat. Maggran's body and soul have been heavily worn by a lifetime of combat, and the quiet mountain sun offers him a measure of healing.",["al"]={"why is maggran here","maggran background","cairne and maggran"},["q"]="Why was Maggran sent to Sun Rock Retreat?"},{["a"]="Maggran directs defense efforts against the savage Bloodfury harpies infesting the mountains and sends warriors to eliminate the giant spider matriarch Besseleth, a terrifying predator he narrowly escaped earlier in his travels.",["al"]={"maggran quests","what does maggran want","harpies stonetalon"},["q"]="What threats does Maggran ask adventurers to deal with?"},{["a"]="Maggran was previously bitten by the colossal spider Besseleth. Though he managed to fend her off and escape with his life, he sends capable adventurers to slay the beast so no one else falls victim to her web.",["al"]={"maggran besseleth","spider quest maggran","arachnophobia lore"},["q"]="What happened between Maggran and Besseleth?"},{["a"]="Maggran serves directly at the behest of Thunder Bluff's High Chieftain, Cairne Bloodhoof. While stationed out in the field at Sun Rock Retreat, his authority and orders stem straight from the capital.",["al"]={"maggran thunder bluff","maggran cairne"},["q"]="Does Maggran have a role in Thunder Bluff?"},{["a"]="No. Maggran is a staunch leader of the Horde and remains fully hostile to any Alliance adventurers who stumble into Sun Rock Retreat.",["al"]={"can alliance talk to maggran","maggran hostile"},["q"]="Is Maggran Earthbinder friendly to Alliance players?"}},["kw"]={"besseleth","bloodfury","cairne bloodhoof","earthbinder","harpies","maggran","stonetalon","sun rock retreat"},["n"]="Maggran Earthbinder",["s"]="Maggran Earthbinder is a grizzled tauren veteran appointed by High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof to lead the Horde encampment at Sun Rock Retreat. Hardened by a lifetime of brutal conflict, he oversees the defense of the craggy valleys of Stonetalon against ravenous beasts and aggressive harpy covens. Though wearied by countless battles, he remains a steadfast guardian of the settlement.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Maggran Earthbinder was sent into the Stonetalon Mountains by High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof himself. A veteran of countless skirmishes and bloody campaigns, Maggran admits that age and violence have hardened his heart, stripping away the natural gentleness typical of his people. Sun Rock Retreat was meant to be both an outpost under his steady command and a place of respite, where warm winds and mountain sunshine might soothe his battle-worn spirit.",["t"]="A Veteran's Haven"},{["b"]="Even in Stonetalon, Maggran finds little peace. As overseer of Sun Rock Retreat, he coordinates defense efforts against the Bloodfury harpies nesting in the peaks and marshals fighters to counter predatory perils across the crags. Having once survived an ambush by the giant spider Besseleth herself, Maggran holds no illusions about the deadly wilderness around them and frequently enlists travelers to eliminate deadly regional predators before they overrun the outpost.",["t"]="Threats in the Crags"}}}}}
t["npc:magistrate-sevren"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,260,24.369.0,19.396.0,25.236.0,37.78.0,46.209.0,39.102.0,53.204.0,50.212.0",["h"]="3ec424",["n"]="Magistrado Sevren",["s"]="Magistrado Sevren. El Magistrado Sevren es el principal funcionario administrativo que preside el asentamiento de Rémol en los Claros de Tirisfal. Desde el interior del ayuntamiento, organiza la defensa inicial de los Renegados y guía a los campeones recién llegados para estabilizar el territorio alrededor de Entrañas. Operando desde el ayuntamiento de Rémol, el Magistrado Sevren coordina la autoridad civil y los esfuerzos estratégicos en las tierras situadas justo al norte de Entrañas. A medida que nuevos Renegados se adentran en los Claros de Tirisfal, Sevren evalúa las crisis locales y envía aventureros para restablecer el orden, asegurar las infraestructuras en ruinas y erradicar las persistentes amenazas que acechan en las colinas circundantes.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Allies of the Horde arriving in Tirisfal will find Sevren coordinating the front-line pacification of Tirisfal Glades against bandits, Scourge remnants, and rebel factions.",["race:Undead"]="For newly liberated Forsaken leaving Deathknell, Magistrate Sevren represents the civic face of Sylvanas's realm, providing your first major assignments to safeguard your homeland."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Magistrate Sevren is the administrative head of Brill, stationed within the town hall. He serves as an overseer for Forsaken territorial management, handing out tasks to adventurers who arrive from Deathknell to aid the fledgling realm.",["al"]={"magistrate sevren","who is sevren","brill magistrate"},["q"]="Who is Magistrate Sevren?"},{["a"]="He is located inside the Town Hall in the center of Brill, in Tirisfal Glades.",["al"]={"sevren location","where is magistrate sevren","find sevren"},["q"]="Where can Magistrate Sevren be found?"},{["a"]="Sevren contends with local threats to Tirisfal Glades, including human graverobbers, rogue rot hides, Scourge remnants desecrating local crypts, and rogue undead figures who refuse allegiance to Lady Sylvanas.",["al"]={"sevren quests","what does sevren want","brill problems"},["q"]="What threats does Magistrate Sevren deal with?"},{["a"]="He is loyal to the Forsaken and governs Brill on behalf of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Undercity.",["al"]={"sevren faction","who does sevren serve"},["q"]="What is Magistrate Sevren's allegiance?"},{["a"]="The crypts belonging to the old Agamand dynasty are overrun with undead and scavenging threats. Sevren demands that adventurers secure the ancestral resting places to prevent enemies from exploiting them.",["al"]={"agamand crypt","sevren crypt quest"},["q"]="Why does Sevren send adventurers to the family crypt?"},{["a"]="Yes. As the local magistrate, he frequently liaises with agents and officials from the Undercity, dispatching messengers and directing adventurers deeper into the capital once their competence in Brill is proven.",["al"]={"sevren undercity","sevren raleigh"},["q"]="Does Sevren have ties to the Undercity leadership?"}},["kw"]={"agamand","brill","forsaken","magistrate","sevren","tirisfal","town hall","undercity"},["n"]="Magistrate Sevren",["s"]="Magistrate Sevren is the chief administrative official presiding over the settlement of Brill in Tirisfal Glades. Standing inside the town hall, he organizes early Forsaken defense and directs arriving champions to stabilize the territory around the Undercity.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Operating from the town hall in Brill, Magistrate Sevren coordinates civil authority and strategic efforts in the lands just north of the Undercity. As new Forsaken step forth into Tirisfal Glades, Sevren assesses local crises and dispatches adventurers to restore order, secure ruined infrastructure, and suppress persistent threats lingering in the surrounding hills.",["t"]="Town Magistrate of Brill"},{["b"]="Sevren's primary concerns center on the preservation and recovery of the Tirisfal dead. Local graverobbers, rot hides, and rogue undead disrupt burial grounds, threatening the emerging dominion of Sylvanas Windrunner. Sevren ensures that ancestral tombs—such as the Agamand Family Crypt—are reclaimed and that deserters or uncooperative forces do not subvert Forsaken authority in the region.",["t"]="Securing the Graves"}}}}}
t["npc:magistrate-solomon"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,281,18.445.0,20.447.0,19.458.1,26.257.0,44.300.1,31.224.1,37.213.0,42.241.0,57.292.0",["h"]="ba5f66",["n"]="Magistrado Salomón",["s"]="Magistrado Salomón. El Magistrado Salomón es el gobernante electo y magistrado principal de Villa del Lago, y preside los asuntos locales desde el ayuntamiento. Asediado por los orcos Roca Negra e implacables clanes de gnolls, pasa sus días suplicando con desesperación ayuda militar a una Ventormenta indiferente y distraída. El Magistrado Salomón gobierna Villa del Lago durante la hora más oscura de su historia reciente. El tranquilo asentamiento a orillas del lago está rodeado de hostilidad: los gnolls Crestagrana y Pellejo Sombrío merodean por las colinas circundantes, mientras que los orcos Roca Negra descienden desde el norte en partidas de guerra organizadas. Salomón trabaja junto al Alguacil Marris para mantener el orden civil y organizar una defensa, pero la milicia y los guardias locales de Villa del Lago están al límite de sus fuerzas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,1,1,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Solomon's political abandonment illustrates the deep fractures within the Alliance of Stormwind, showing how outer provinces are left entirely to rely on freelance heroes.",["race:Dwarf"]="Dwarven visitors may find a tragic connection in Solomon's history, as Ironforge's effort to answer his distress call resulted in the ambush and capture of Princess Moira Bronzebeard.",["race:Human"]="For human travelers, speaking to Solomon reveals the grim state of the kingdom outside the safety of Elwynn Forest's inner borders."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Magistrate Solomon is the elected civil leader of Lakeshire and presiding judge of the Court of Lakeshire. Operating from the town hall, he oversees local administrative matters and orchestrates the town's desperate defense against invading gnolls and orcs.",["al"]={"magistrate solomon lore","who is solomon","lakeshire leader"},["q"]="Who is Magistrate Solomon?"},{["a"]="Stormwind's military is already stretched thin across several troubled regions. When Solomon appeals for aid, Highlord Bolvar Fordragon is heavily influenced by royal advisor Lady Katrana Prestor, who questions Solomon's reports and actively discourages committing regular kingdom troops to Redridge.",["al"]={"why no stormwind army","why won't stormwind help lakeshire","bolvar aid redridge"},["q"]="Why can't Stormwind send troops to help him?"},{["a"]="Yes. At Solomon's plea, King Magni Bronzebeard dispatched a relief contingent headed by Princess Moira Bronzebeard. However, the expedition never made it to Redridge, having been ambushed and captured in the Burning Steppes.",["al"]={"dwarf reinforcements lakeshire","ironforge help redridge","moira bronzebeard lakeshire"},["q"]="Did Ironforge try to send help?"},{["a"]="Lakeshire faces simultaneous pressure from the Redridge and Shadowhide gnolls who terrorize the hills and roads, as well as the aggressive Blackrock orcs raiding south from Stonewatch Keep and the Burning Steppes.",["al"]={"what is attacking lakeshire","redridge enemies","why is solomon worried"},["q"]="What threats are troubling Lakeshire?"},{["a"]="Solomon coordinates primarily with Marshal Marris, who directs the local town guard. Because regular reinforcements never arrive, the two officials are forced to enlist and deputize traveling adventurers to push back the encroaching threats.",["al"]={"lakeshire defenders","marshal marris and solomon"},["q"]="Who works with Solomon to defend the town?"},{["a"]="Knowing Stormwind's court has stalled, Solomon attempts to form mutual aid pacts with neighboring Alliance settlements. Unfortunately, Westfall is paralyzed by the Defias Brotherhood and Darkshire is overwhelmed by the undead and feral beasts, leaving neither able to spare a single defender.",["al"]={"messenger to darkshire","messenger to westfall","solomon aid other towns"},["q"]="Why does Solomon send couriers to Darkshire and Westfall?"}},["kw"]={"blackrock","bolvar","lakeshire","magistrate solomon","marris","prestor","redridge","solomon","town hall"},["n"]="Magistrate Solomon",["s"]="Magistrate Solomon is the elected ruler and chief magistrate of Lakeshire, presiding over local affairs from the town hall. Besieged by Blackrock orcs and relentless gnoll clans, he spends his days frantically pleading for military aid from an indifferent and distracted Stormwind.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Magistrate Solomon governs Lakeshire during the darkest hour in its recent history. The tranquil lakeside settlement is surrounded by hostility: Redridge and Shadowhide gnolls prowl the surrounding hills, while Blackrock orcs descend from the north in organized warbands. Solomon works alongside Marshal Marris to maintain civil order and muster a defense, but Lakeshire's local guards and militia are stretched to their absolute breaking point.",["t"]="A Town Under Siege"},{["b"]="Desperate to secure reinforcements, Solomon has dispatched messengers across the kingdom—pleading for aid from Westfall, Darkshire, and the capital of Stormwind itself. His petitions have yielded bitter disappointment. Westfall struggles under the grip of the Defias Brotherhood, Duskwood is consumed by its own creeping terrors, and Stormwind City refuses to deploy troops to the eastern frontier, leaving Lakeshire entirely to its own devices.",["t"]="Appeals to Deaf Ears"},{["b"]="When evidence emerges that the Blackrock orcs are allied with the black dragonflight, Solomon forwards the warning straight to Highlord Bolvar Fordragon. Despite the magnitude of the threat, royal advisor Lady Katrana Prestor dismisses Solomon's pleas as wild exaggeration. Constrained by her counsel and Stormwind's thinly spread forces, Bolvar declines to commit the Stormwind Army, offering Solomon only royal sanction to deputize independent mercenaries.",["t"]="The Court's Refusal"}}}}}
t["npc:magni-bronzebeard"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,280,20.683.0,21.631.0,19.597.0,25.222.0,26.296.0,34.283.0,24.239.0,35.242.0,30.267.0",["h"]="858a0d",["n"]="Magni Barbabronce",["s"]="Magni Barbabronce. Magni Barbabronce es el Señor de Forjaz, thane del clan Barbabronce y gobernante de Khaz Modan. Herrero sin igual y veterano comandante de la Segunda Guerra, lidera su reino montañoso en medio del dolor y la tensión política, a la vez que defiende la arqueología enana por todo Azeroth. Siendo el mayor de tres hermanos, Magni creció muy consciente del peso que le aguardaba bajo la montaña. Cuando la Horda invadió durante la Segunda Guerra, mantuvo Forjaz tras sus impenetrables puertas y salió a comprometer a Khaz Modan con la Alianza de Lordaeron una vez roto el asedio. En los años de paz posteriores, Magni acogió a sus aliados gnomos en la ciudad tras la caída de Gnomeregan, concediendo santuario dentro de la montaña al Manitas Mayor Gelbin Mekkatorque y a sus refugiados. Para unir los fracturados reinos del norte y del sur, Magni pidió a Mekkatorque que diseñara una maravilla subterránea sin precedentes: el Tren subterráneo, que conecta directamente Forjaz con Ventormenta.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="A stalwart founder of the Grand Alliance alongside Lordaeron and Stormwind, Magni provides martial strength, engineering prowess, and steadfast loyalty to the coalition.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Magni is considered one of the greatest living smiths on Azeroth, having shaped the fabled Ashbringer from an otherworldly crystal at Ironforge's Great Anvil.",["race:Dwarf"]="Magni is your undisputed sovereign and the protector of Khaz Modan, leading the Bronzebeard clan through external wars and the internal search for your race's earthen heritage.",["race:Gnome"]="King Magni offered his city as a refuge to the survivors of Gnomeregan, maintaining a close friendship and technological alliance with High Tinker Mekkatorque."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Magni Bronzebeard is the King of Khaz Modan, Thane of Ironforge, and chieftain of the Bronzebeard clan. He rules the mountain kingdom from the High Seat in Ironforge and is one of the staunch pillars of the Grand Alliance.",["al"]={"king of ironforge","dwarf king","who is magni"},["q"]="Who is Magni Bronzebeard?"},{["a"]="King Magni forged the legendary sword himself at the Great Anvil in Ironforge. Alexandros Mograine and High Inquisitor Fairbanks brought him an enigmatic crystal of living Light, and Magni poured his grief and fury over Muradin's reported death into the blade over three days of nonstop smithing.",["al"]={"did magni make ashbringer","ashbringer creator","who made the ashbringer"},["q"]="Who forged the Ashbringer?"},{["a"]="Magni is the eldest of three brothers. His brother Muradin served as an Alliance ambassador to Lordaeron and was reported killed by Prince Arthas in Northrend. His youngest brother, Brann, is a renowned explorer who travels the far corners of the world leading the Explorers' League.",["al"]={"muradin and brann","magni brothers","muradin bronzebeard fate"},["q"]="What happened to Magni's brothers?"},{["a"]="Princess Moira Bronzebeard, Magni's only child, has disappeared from Ironforge. Official reports within the mountain hold that she was abducted by the antagonistic Dark Iron dwarves and is being held captive deep within Blackrock Mountain.",["al"]={"magni daughter","where is moira","what happened to moira bronzebeard"},["q"]="Where is Princess Moira?"},{["a"]="Following the trogg invasion and horrific irradiation of Gnomeregan, King Magni opened Ironforge's gates to High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque and the gnomish survivors. Magni granted them an entire district of the city, now known as Tinker Town.",["al"]={"tinker town","why are gnomes in the dwarf city","gnome refugees ironforge"},["q"]="Why are gnomes living in Ironforge?"},{["a"]="The Explorers' League is an archaeological organization founded by King Magni and his brother Brann. After discovering ancient titan ruins, Magni directed dwarven industries toward uncovering the truth behind their race's origins, sending survey teams across Azeroth.",["al"]={"explorers guild","dwarf archaeologists","why are dwarves digging"},["q"]="What is the Explorers' League?"}},["kw"]={"ashbringer","brann","bronzebeard","explorers league","ironforge","khaz modan","magni","moira","muradin"},["n"]="Magni Bronzebeard",["s"]="Magni Bronzebeard is the Lord of Ironforge, Thane of the Bronzebeard clan, and ruler of Khaz Modan. A peerless smith and veteran commander of the Second War, he leads his mountainous kingdom through grief and political tension while championing dwarven archaeology across Azeroth.",["sec"]={{["b"]="The eldest of three brothers, Magni grew up keenly aware of the weight awaiting him under the mountain. When the Horde invaded during the Second War, he held Ironforge behind its impenetrable gates, emerging to pledge Khaz Modan to the Alliance of Lordaeron once the siege was broken. In the years of peace that followed, Magni welcomed his gnomish allies into the city after the fall of Gnomeregan, granting High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque and his refugees sanctuary within the mountain. To unite the fractured southern and northern kingdoms, Magni petitioned Mekkatorque to engineer an unprecedented subterranean marvel: the Deeprun Tram, connecting Ironforge directly to Stormwind.",["t"]="Lord of the Mountain"},{["b"]="Beneath Magni's regal bearing lies deep personal tragedy. During the Third War, word arrived from Northrend that Prince Arthas Menethil had betrayed and murdered Magni's beloved younger brother, Muradin. Overwhelmed by sorrow and wrath, Magni took up his hammer at the Great Anvil when High Inquisitor Fairbanks and Alexandros Mograine brought him a crystal of pure, radiant Light. Over three tireless days, the dwarven king poured all his grief, rage, and desire for vengeance into the metal. The resulting blade—the Ashbringer—stands as the greatest masterwork of his lifetime, forged to bring ruin to Arthas and the Scourge.",["t"]="A Hammer of Vengeance"},{["b"]="Under Magni's decree, dwarven society has turned much of its focus away from traditional commercial mining toward the unearthing of ancient history. Spurred by discoveries of strange titan relics deep beneath the earth, Magni co-founded the Explorers' League alongside his surviving brother, Brann Bronzebeard. Dwarven dig sites now dot the continents, from Dun Morogh to Kalimdor, striving to unlock the mystery of how the earthen became the modern dwarf. However, domestic peace remains fragile: Magni's daughter, Princess Moira, has gone missing, believed kidnapped by the hated Dark Iron clan.",["t"]="Excavating the Past"}}}}}
t["npc:makaba-flathoof"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,291,23.401.0,20.378.1,23.189.0,27.144.0,30.141.0,46.199.0,22.152.0,34.172.0",["h"]="20f277",["n"]="Makaba Patatleta",["s"]="Makaba Patatleta. Makaba Patatleta es un tauren superviviente originario de Campamento Aparaje en Sierra Espolón. Tras presenciar la devastación de su hogar y de su pueblo a manos del clan Tótem Siniestro, busca a valientes campeones de la Horda para vengarse de los atacantes y garantizar la seguridad de su familia. Makaba Patatleta personifica el trágico precio de las luchas internas entre los tauren. Su hogar, Campamento Aparaje en Sierra Espolón, fue víctima de un despiadado ataque sorpresa por parte del clan Tótem Siniestro. Mientras que muchos tauren luchan por la paz y la unidad bajo el liderazgo de Cairne Pezuña de Sangre, los traicioneros Tótem Siniestro siembran continuamente la discordia y la violencia, dejando a supervivientes como Makaba desplazados y sumidos en el dolor.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Makaba's calls for aid allow Horde champions to prove their loyalty to their tauren allies by punishing those who butcher peaceful encampments.",["race:Tauren"]="For tauren heroes, Makaba's plight highlights the bitter treachery of the Grimtotem, serving as a reminder that not all of their kin honor the ways of peace and unity."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Makaba Flathoof is a tauren refugee from Camp Aparaje in the Stonetalon Mountains. His village was overrun and sacked by the Grimtotem clan, driving him to seek help from Horde adventurers.",["al"]={"makaba","who is makaba flathoof","makaba flathoof lore"},["q"]="Who is Makaba Flathoof?"},{["a"]="Makaba hails from Camp Aparaje, a small tauren settlement located in the Stonetalon Mountains that was attacked and devastated by the Grimtotem.",["al"]={"makaba origin","where is makaba from","camp aparaje makaba"},["q"]="Where did Makaba come from?"},{["a"]="Camp Aparaje was sacked by the Grimtotem clan, an aggressive and treacherous faction of tauren led locally by figures like Grundig Darkcloud.",["al"]={"who attacked camp aparaje","makaba enemies","who sacked aparaje"},["q"]="Who attacked Makaba's village?"},{["a"]="Makaba seeks vengeance for his fallen home, asking capable warriors to cut down the Grimtotem forces at Camp Aparaje, eliminate their leader Grundig Darkcloud, and discover the fate of Kaya Flathoof.",["al"]={"makaba quests","what does makaba ask for","makaba tasks"},["q"]="What does Makaba want Horde adventurers to do?"},{["a"]="Kaya Flathoof is a relative of Makaba who went missing during the attack on Camp Aparaje. Makaba desperately hopes to learn if she survived the assault.",["al"]={"kaya flathoof","who is kaya","makaba relative kaya"},["q"]="Who is Kaya to Makaba?"},{["a"]="Both Makaba and Dim share the Flathoof family surname, indicating they are part of the same tauren lineage, though their specific degree of relation is not deeply detailed.",["al"]={"dim flathoof","makaba and dim","flathoof family"},["q"]="Is Makaba related to Dim Flathoof?"}},["kw"]={"camp aparaje","flathoof","grimtotem","grundig darkcloud","kaya","makaba","stonetalon"},["n"]="Makaba Flathoof",["s"]="Makaba Flathoof is a tauren survivor hailing from Camp Aparaje in the Stonetalon Mountains. Having witnessed the devastation of his home and people at the hands of the Grimtotem clan, he seeks brave champions of the Horde to bring vengeance upon the attackers and ensure his family's safety.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Makaba Flathoof represents the tragic toll of internal strife among the tauren. His home, Camp Aparaje in the Stonetalon Mountains, fell victim to a ruthless surprise attack by the Grimtotem clan. While many tauren strive for peace and unity under the leadership of Cairne Bloodhoof, the treacherous Grimtotem continually sow discord and violence, leaving survivors like Makaba displaced and grieving.",["t"]="Tragedy at Camp Aparaje"},{["b"]="Unable to retake his fallen settlement alone, Makaba calls upon travelers of the Horde to strike back. He directs fierce retaliation against the Grimtotem renegades who overran his home, demanding justice for the slaughter of his kin. His most urgent concerns center on confronting the warlord responsible, Grundig Darkcloud, and finding word of his missing family member, Kaya.",["t"]="A Plea for Vengeance"}}}}}
